मण्डलम् शृङ्खला ॥   ॰ shrinkhala — the DRIVER, the port of crates/sadhana/src/t1/chain.rs

॰ THE TOP OF THE GRAPH, AND THAT IS WHY IT IS ITS OWN MODULE. Every other
॰ module here is called BY this one; nothing calls it. Putting the driver inside
॰ `यन्त्रोत्सर्जन` — the only module that already reaches the emitter — would
॰ have made the EMITTER import parse and resolve, so that something above both
॰ could call them. An inverted edge is permanent and a loader line is one line.
॰
॰ WHAT IT IS THE PORT OF, AND WHAT IT IS DELIBERATELY NOT. `chain.rs` is 1005
॰ lines. 83 are its header, 233 are the stage sequence this file ports, and the
॰ remaining 689 — `Built`, `read_module`, `binary_kind`, and the accessors
॰ `global_int`/`global_bool`/`global_text`/`arena`/`token_text`/`member`/
॰ `int_of`/`set_int`/`id_of`/`arena_int` — exist to move data ACROSS the
॰ boundary between Rust and the interpreter. A driver written in `.t1` is
॰ already on the far side of that boundary: it reads `आज्ञाकोश` where the Rust
॰ one marshals it into a `Vec<Instruction>`. So 69% of that file has no
॰ counterpart here, for the same reason `kosha.t1` is a tenth of `kosha.rs` —
॰ the Rust side serves a consumer this side does not have.
॰
॰ AND `chain.rs` IS NOT A NINETEEN-SOURCE WALKER, which is worth saying because
॰ its row was scoped as one. It has no loop over sources at all; `t1_build`
॰ drives it a source at a time and the corpus walk lives in the censuses.

आयातः पदविभाग ।
आयातः व्याकर ।
आयातः अर्थ ।
॰ THE DECLARATION STORE. Imported for `सङ्ग्रहः` below, and the reason it was
॰ not here before is the defect this fixes: the store was filled by the RUST
॰ driver and not by this one.
आयातः घोषणासञ्चय ।
आयातः मध्यरूप ।
आयातः यन्त्रोत्सर्जन ।
आयातः वाक्यविभाग ।   ॰ the Sassembly reader — the emitted text goes back in here
आयातः सङ्केतन ।      ॰ the encoder, and the object builder that W-279 added
आयातः संयोजन ।       ॰ the linker
आयातः कोश ।          ॰ the image writer
॰ AND `वास्तु`, WHICH THE BACK HALF NAMES AND THE FIRST VERSION DID NOT IMPORT.
॰ `पाठवस्तुरचना` answers a `वास्तुॱवस्तु` and `वस्तुप्रतिबिम्बम्` takes one, so
॰ this file reaches that module at four sites. EVERY TEST PASSED WITHOUT IT —
॰ `वास्तु` is in `CHAIN`, so the qualified name resolves at run time and nothing
॰ faults. What was missing was the DECLARATION, not the module, and only a
॰ checker that reads imports rather than runs code can see the difference.
आयातः वास्तु ।       ॰ the object record the back half builds and links
आयातः अष्टक ।        ॰ the OUTPUT CHANNEL — `मुद्रणम्`, and nothing else here uses it
आयातः समावेशसारणी ।   ॰ the generated spec-table store (tools/mkspectables.py)

आयातः अक्षरकोश ।     ॰ R-15-1's repertoire — W-304: `पठनम्` lexes through `परिधिपदविभाग`

॰ ॥ THE REPERTOIRE REFUSAL ॥ did the last SOURCE lexed meet a code point outside
॰ R-15-1, and at which octet: `अक्षरकोशॱपरिधिदोषस्थितम्` and `परिधिदोषस्थानम्`.
॰ They lived HERE until 2026-10-01 (W-304, a peer session's placement ruling), when
॰ the gate moved out of `पठनम्` into `अक्षरकोशॱपरिधिपदविभाग` — the ONE gated
॰ source entry, which `chain.rs`'s `Front::lex` also calls, so the driver that
॰ never reaches `पठनम्` is gated too. `पठनम्` answers ० for this AND for "no
॰ declarations", so a reader asks those two globals, exactly as
॰ `निर्णयविरामभेद` is asked.

॰ How many objects the last `मण्डलानिप्रतिबिम्बम्` collected — the startup plus
॰ every source that produced one. A caller cannot recover this from the image,
॰ and a test asserting "twenty sources went in" without asking how many objects
॰ came OUT would pass over a driver that silently skipped nineteen of them. It
॰ is set BEFORE the link, so it reports what was collected even when the link
॰ refuses: "nothing was collected" and "the link failed" need different fixes
॰ and a success-only counter cannot tell them apart.
॰
॰ AND THE SENTENCE ABOVE IS TRUE OF THE LINK AND FALSE OF THE TWO EARLY RETURNS
॰ ABOVE IT. A startup that does not emit, and a startup text that does not
॰ assemble, both return before this is ever written — leaving the initial ०,
॰ which is exactly what "collected nothing" looks like. IT IS A COUNTER PLACED
॰ TO SURVIVE ONE FAILURE MODE, SITTING BELOW TWO IT CANNOT SEE. It earned its
॰ place on its first run — `Some(0)` against twenty enumerated sources is what
॰ said the startup path bailed before the loop — but it did so by luck of which
॰ path fired, and a reader must not take ० here as "the corpus produced no
॰ objects". Ask `अन्तिमवस्तुदोषः` before believing this number.
सार्वजनिक चरः संयोजितवस्तुसंख्या ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।

॰ HOW MANY SOURCES DID NOT REACH AN OBJECT, counted as each one compiles and
॰ read once after the loop. `संयोजितवस्तुसंख्या` says how many objects went INTO
॰ the link; this says how many sources did not produce one. Without it a corpus
॰ where three sources refuse and a corpus where none does both answer "linked",
॰ because a refusing source was dropped in silence — the two need different
॰ fixes and they were the same number.
सार्वजनिक चरः सङ्कलनविफलसंख्या ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।
॰ THE FIRST FAILED SOURCE'S CAUSE, for the trace level ३ dump of `स्वपरीक्षास्वप्रतिबिम्बम्`:
॰ its `सङ्कलनविरामभेद` and, for `सङ्कलनवर्गविरोधभेद`, `मध्यरूप`'s shape (७ = फलपलायननिषेधः,
॰ 0x377; ८ = क्षेत्रबाह्याह्वाननिषेधः, 0x37F; ९ = क्षेत्राशुद्धाह्वाननिषेधः, 0x381; १० = संश्लिष्टनामनिषेधः, 0x382),
॰ taken when it fails because the next source overwrites both.
सार्वजनिक चरः प्रथमविफलविरामभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।
सार्वजनिक चरः प्रथमविफलवर्गविरोधभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।

॰ THE SOURCES THAT DECLARED NOTHING, WHICH ARE NOT FAILURES (2026-09-22).
॰ `मण्डलसङ्कलनम्` already tells the two apart — `सङ्कलनाघोषणाभेद` (१) is "the
॰ source parsed to no declarations" and `सङ्कलनानिर्णयभेद` (२) is "`अर्थ` refused
॰ it" — but this rung read only the emitted text's length, so `lib.t1`, which
॰ holds no declaration ON PURPOSE (its own margin says so), was counted a
॰ failure in every build this repository has ever run: "1 source(s) failed to
॰ compile (lib)". A count with a floor cannot express its zero, and this one
॰ could never read ०. Measured 2026-09-22 on `lib.t1`: `सङ्कलनविरामभेद = १`,
॰ `निर्णयविरामभेद = ३` (अर्थ was never entered).
सार्वजनिक चरः सङ्कलनरिक्तसंख्या ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।
॰ ॥ AND WHICH ONES ॥ (2026-09-14) A COUNT IS NOT THE NAMES. The margin above
॰ argued the counter into existence because a refusing source was dropped in
॰ silence — and then eighteen self-images in a row read `1`, which nobody could
॰ act on without already knowing whether `1` was normal. It was: `lib.t1` is
॰ 1,141 octets of margin with ZERO code lines, so there is nothing in it to
॰ compile and never was, and the counter has a permanent floor of 1. That floor
॰ is worse than it sounds: the one thing the counter was built to say — "every
॰ source compiled" — is the one thing it can no longer express, and a genuine
॰ new failure reads `2`.
॰ The other repair was to skip a source whose code half is empty, which buys a
॰ zero by teaching the instrument to look away from a file; the next real
॰ failure would still arrive as a bare number. The name answers both, and it
॰ answers the general case: `नाम` is already in scope at the failure arm.
सार्वजनिक चरः सङ्कलनविफलनामकोश ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति ० ।
॰ THE SELF-IMAGE'S ENTRY, 2026-09-13. `मण्डलानिप्रतिबिम्बम्` names no entry, so the
॰ compiler's own image halts at the startup stub. A caller may name one here —
॰ (module, routine) — and the routine is registered in the emitter's name table
॰ under a private symbol just before the startup is emitted, after the last
॰ module's `नामसञ्चयः` has reset that table. `स्वपरीक्षा` below is the first
॰ entry worth naming: it takes no arguments and returns a number the
॰ interpreted chain can predict.
सार्वजनिक चरः प्रवेशमस्ति ॱॱ बूल भवति असत्यम् ।
सार्वजनिक चरः प्रवेशमण्डलम् ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति ० ।
सार्वजनिक चरः प्रवेशवृत्तिः ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति ० ।
सार्वजनिक चरः प्रवेशसंज्ञा ॱॱ न६४ भवति १००००००० ।

॰ W-280 — WHICH EXIT `मण्डलसङ्कलनम्` TOOK. It has six ways out and answered the
॰ SAME OCTETS from five of them: `रिक्तम्`, empty, recording nothing. So a module
॰ that legitimately emits no code and a module that was refused were one answer,
॰ and `kosha_end_to_end.rs:838` had already written that down — *"the whole-call
॰ empty answer names nothing"*.
॰
॰ THE INSTANCE IS `वास्तु`, NOT A HYPOTHETICAL. `ast.t1` and `vastu.t1` declare
॰ one module between them with 45 globals, 8 types and **zero routines**, so
॰ `वृत्तयः समम् ०` fires on a module that is entirely data. It is in `CHAIN` and
॰ seven loaded modules import it.
॰
॰ EACH EXIT GETS ITS OWN VALUE, not a success/failure bit. A discriminator that
॰ separated "emitted nothing" from the other four LUMPED TOGETHER would let
॰ `वास्तु` through and leave the defect for the next module.
॰ **INITIALISED TO THE SENTINEL (६), NOT TO ० — WHICH IS `सङ्कलनसिद्धभेद`.**
॰ The routine resets to `सङ्कलनानारब्धभेद` on entry, so this initial value is read
॰ only BEFORE the first call — and it was ०, meaning a reader that asked before
॰ anything ran was told "emitted". Fail-open in exactly the place W-280 chose a
॰ sentinel to avoid it. `वस्तुरचनाविरामभेद` was already declared at its own
॰ sentinel ४; these two were inconsistent and the inconsistency was invisible
॰ because each looked right beside its own constants.
॰ The literal ६ and not the name: `सङ्कलनानारब्धभेद` is declared below this line.
सार्वजनिक चरः सङ्कलनविरामभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ६ ।

सार्वजनिक चरः सङ्कलनसिद्धभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।        ॰ emitted
सार्वजनिक चरः सङ्कलनाघोषणाभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति १ ।       ॰ the source parsed to no declarations
सार्वजनिक चरः सङ्कलनानिर्णयभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति २ ।      ॰ अर्थ refused it
सार्वजनिक चरः सङ्कलनावृत्तिभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ३ ।      ॰ NO ROUTINES — data only, not an error
सार्वजनिक चरः सङ्कलननामवैषम्यभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ४ ।    ॰ names attempted ≠ entries written

॰ **A MISMATCH EXIT IS ONE NUMBER WHERE THE QUESTION NEEDS THREE.** Exit ४ says
॰ the two counts differ and cannot say by how much or in which direction, and
॰ those decide whether the appender lost entries or the guard is counting a
॰ population that was never nameable. Both are recorded so a reader never has to
॰ re-run the front half to find out.
सार्वजनिक चरः सङ्कलननामप्रयासाः ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।     ॰ attempted, last मण्डलसङ्कलनम्
सार्वजनिक चरः सङ्कलननामप्रविष्टयः ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।   ॰ written, last मण्डलसङ्कलनम्
सार्वजनिक चरः सङ्कलनानामभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ५ ।         ॰ no name was recorded at all

॰ THE SENTINEL, AND IT IS THE DEFAULT THAT MAKES THIS FIX FAIL-CLOSED. A first
॰ version reset to `सङ्कलनसिद्धभेद` — ०, "emitted" — so ANY return that did not
॰ set the code would have reported SUCCESS. That is correct while all six
॰ returns set it and silent the moment a seventh is added, **which is exactly
॰ the defect this row exists for**: `मण्डलसङ्कलनम्` accumulated five silent
॰ returns over time, two of them added in the fold hours before this.
॰
॰ Resetting to ६ means an unrecorded exit is a value NO CALLER EXPECTS rather
॰ than the value every caller reads as fine. The cost is one assignment on the
॰ success path; the gain is that the next silent return is loud.
सार्वजनिक चरः सङ्कलनानारब्धभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ६ ।      ॰ no exit was recorded — a defect
॰ ROUTINES WERE BUILT AND NO TEXT CAME BACK. Distinct from `सङ्कलनावृत्तिभेद` (३),
॰ which is a module with NO routines and is not an error: `ast.t1` and `vastu.t1`
॰ declare none, emit nothing, and are correct. This is the contradiction — a
॰ module that built routines and emitted zero octets, which until 2026-09-15
॰ reported `सङ्कलनसिद्धभेद` and was counted as a success by everything downstream.
सार्वजनिक चरः सङ्कलनानुत्सर्जनभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ७ ।   ॰ built routines, emitted nothing
॰ W-345 — THE SOURCE NEVER LEXED: an octet outside R-15-1, refused by
॰ `अक्षरकोशॱपरिधिपदविभाग` before a single token was written. Until this value
॰ existed the exit was recorded as `सङ्कलनाघोषणाभेद` (१), because `पठनम्`
॰ answers ० tokens and ० declarations alike and the caller read only the
॰ count — so a corpus walk filed a repertoire-refused source under "declared
॰ nothing, not a failure" and `t1_boot --object` exited SUCCESS on it. The
॰ octet is at `अक्षरकोशॱपरिधिदोषस्थानम्`, meaningful while `परिधिदोषस्थितम्`
॰ stands; `chain::refusal_site` renders both.
सार्वजनिक चरः सङ्कलनपरिधिभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ८ ।        ॰ an octet outside R-15-1 — never lexed
॰ W-342 — THE PARSER REFUSED IT. The third cause behind `पठनम्`'s ०, and until
॰ this value existed it too was recorded as `सङ्कलनाघोषणाभेद` (१): measured on
॰ `393532c5`, a source refused at line ३ built with no entry printed "0
॰ source(s) failed to compile, 1 declared nothing", wrote an image of the
॰ startup alone and exited ZERO. The record is `व्याकरॱदोषकोश`, १ to
॰ `व्याकरॱदोषसूचकाङ्क` — line, column and reason — and it is this source's
॰ own because `पठनम्` resets the count before the gate.
सार्वजनिक चरः सङ्कलनव्याकरणभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ९ ।      ॰ the parser refused it — tokens, no program

॰ `W-359` — THE LOWERING COULD NOT BOUND A PARAMETER STORE. `मध्यरूप` counts a
॰ store into a guarded run parameter it cannot bound (no element width, or a
॰ slot past its mask) in `मध्यरूपॱप्राचलरक्षादोषसंख्या` instead of emitting the
॰ unbounded store, and the module is refused here, after `रचना`.
सार्वजनिक चरः सङ्कलनप्राचलरक्षाभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति १० ।
॰ `V-005`: `मध्यरूप` refused a value crossing into a declared file it is not in.
सार्वजनिक चरः सङ्कलनवर्गविरोधभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ११ ।

॰ W-279 — WHICH EXIT `पाठवस्तुरचना` TOOK. The same defect as `सङ्कलनविरामभेद`
॰ one layer down: four ways out and `शून्यम्` from three of them, so a module
॰ that assembled nothing DELIBERATELY and a module whose reader failed were one
॰ answer. `मण्डलानिप्रतिबिम्बम्` reads that `शून्यम्` and cannot say which.
॰
॰ FOUR EXITS, NOT SIX; FIVE SINCE W-302 (५, the splitter refused). One is not constructible — see the test.
॰ THE SENTINEL IS THE DEFAULT, for the reason W-280's was: a return that
॰ forgets to record reports a value NO CALLER EXPECTS rather than "built".
सार्वजनिक चरः वस्तुरचनाविरामभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ४ ।

सार्वजनिक चरः वस्तुरचनासिद्धभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।     ॰ an object was built
सार्वजनिक चरः वस्तुरचनावाक्यभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति १ ।    ॰ the text parsed to no statements
सार्वजनिक चरः वस्तुरचनारिक्तभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति २ ।    ॰ statements, but NOTHING was built
सार्वजनिक चरः वस्तुरचनाष्टकभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ३ ।     ॰ encoding refused — see सङ्केतनदोष
सार्वजनिक चरः वस्तुरचनानारब्धभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ४ ।   ॰ no exit recorded — a defect
सार्वजनिक चरः वस्तुरचनावाक्यदोषभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ५ ।  ॰ W-302: the splitter refused a statement — see वाक्यविभागदोषकोश

॰ THE RESOLVER, KEPT RATHER THAN DISCARDED — and this is the whole reason the
॰ `.t1` chain needed `chain.rs` to name its routines.
॰
॰ `मध्यरूप` pushes every routine with `नाम` = ०, faithfully mirroring
॰ `ir.rs:661/:715/:814` which pushes `SymbolId(0)`. THE SYMBOL IS GENUINELY NOT
॰ AVAILABLE AT IR-BUILD TIME IN EITHER DESIGN. `chain.rs:616` then writes the
॰ real symbol back with the margin "the symbol chosen here is written back where
॰ the T1 emitter reads it" — so on every Rust-orchestrated run `वृत्ति ॱ नाम` is
॰ true by the time anything looks, and a `.t1`-only run had never happened.
॰
॰ THE FIELD IS ONLY VALID DOWNSTREAM OF RUST, AND THAT IS THE DEPENDENCY THIS
॰ REMOVES. It is not a missing compiler stage: `अर्थ` already holds every name
॰ and symbol the mapping needs. What was missing is that `निर्णयः` built the
॰ resolver as a LOCAL and dropped it, so the one structure carrying the answer
॰ did not outlive the stage that made it.
॰
॰ THE DECLARATION IS BELOW, ONCE. It stood here as well until 2026-09-09: this
॰ margin and the one further down were written on two branches that each also
॰ declared the pair, and THE MERGE OF THE TWO WAS CLEAN — the additions landed
॰ in different hunks, so nothing conflicted and `शृङ्खला` declared each global
॰ TWICE. Caught by `the_loader_gives_the_same_program_under_every_order_of_the_
॰ fifteen_sources`, which reported `declared by [शृङ्खला, शृङ्खला]` — a guard
॰ built for collisions BETWEEN modules, firing on one module against itself.

॰ THE RESOLVER IS HELD IN ONE SLOT AND THAT IS A DELIBERATE CHOICE, NOT AN
॰ OVERSIGHT. `निर्णयः` overwrites `निर्णायकधारः` on every call, so THIS HOLDS
॰ THE MOST RECENTLY RESOLVED PROGRAM — per-program is a property of the VALUE
॰ and the HOLDER is a single slot.
॰
॰ TODAY THAT CANNOT BITE: every caller resolves one source and emits it before
॰ resolving another, so resolve-then-emit is the only order that happens. IT
॰ STOPS BEING INVISIBLE AT EXACTLY WHAT THIS ROW IS REACHING FOR — an image
॰ built from twenty sources. A driver that resolves B before emitting A will
॰ have `नामसञ्चयः` reading A's routine names out of B's scopes, first-match
॰ will answer something plausible, and NO COUNT WILL MOVE.
॰
॰ THE PRECEDENT IS `यन्त्रोत्सर्जन`'s, recorded by the lane that hit it: a
॰ global set inside the allocation emitter and read by the startup "answers
॰ correctly only if the body has already been emitted", replaced by a pure scan
॰ because today's agreement would have been evidence rather than structure.
॰ SAME STRUCTURE, DIFFERENT FILE.
॰
॰ Held anyway because `निर्णयः` answers `बूल` and threading the resolver out of
॰ it changes a signature three callers and the toy test depend on. WHEN THE
॰ DRIVER WALKS MORE THAN ONE SOURCE BEFORE EMITTING, THIS BECOMES A DEFECT AND
॰ THE FIX IS TO PASS THE RESOLVER RATHER THAN HOLD IT.
सार्वजनिक चरः निर्णायकधारः ॱॱ अर्थॱनिर्णायक भवति ० ।
सार्वजनिक चरः निर्णायकसिद्धः ॱॱ बूल भवति असत्यम् ।

॰ W-279 — WHICH OF `निर्णयः`'s TWO STAGES REFUSED. Third instance of the same
॰ defect as `सङ्कलनविरामभेद` and `वस्तुरचनाविरामभेद`, and the one that is
॰ currently costing a measurement: the cross-module pair stops with
॰ `सङ्कलनविरामभेद = सङ्कलनानिर्णयभेद` (२), which says only "अर्थ refused" —
॰ `निर्णयः` folds resolve and typecheck into ONE `बूल` and both refusals leave
॰ the caller the same `असत्यम्`. Four runs on 8c444afa narrowed the stop to this
॰ routine and could go no further, because the answer is not in the return
॰ value and never was.
॰
॰ THE SEPARATION IS THE WHOLE POINT, AND IT IS NOT A SUCCESS/FAILURE BIT.
॰ Resolve refusing means a NAME was not found — the callee's symbol never
॰ reached the caller's scope, i.e. `घोषणासञ्चय` or the resolver's cross-module
॰ import path. Typecheck refusing means the name WAS found and its signature
॰ disagreed — a different file, a different fix, and the two were one answer.
॰ The `निर्णयः` margin has claimed since it was written that "the stage that
॰ refused is readable from the module here without threading it through a
॰ return"; nothing made it readable. This does.
॰
॰ SENTINEL-INITIALISED (३), NOT ० — ० IS `निर्णयसिद्धभेद`, "both stages passed".
॰ `सङ्कलनविरामभेद`'s own note records why: a reader that asks before anything
॰ ran must not be told the thing succeeded. The routine resets to the sentinel
॰ on ENTRY as well, for the reason stated at `मण्डलसङ्कलनम्` — without the reset
॰ a second call that returns by an unrecorded path reports the FIRST call's
॰ exit. The literal ३ and not the name: `निर्णयानारब्धभेद` is declared below.
सार्वजनिक चरः निर्णयविरामभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ३ ।

सार्वजनिक चरः निर्णयसिद्धभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।        ॰ resolved AND typechecked
सार्वजनिक चरः निर्णयनिर्णायकभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति १ ।     ॰ अर्थॱकार्यक्रमनिर्णयः refused — RESOLVE
सार्वजनिक चरः निर्णयप्रकारभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति २ ।       ॰ अर्थॱकार्यक्रमप्रकारपरीक्षा refused — TYPECHECK
सार्वजनिक चरः निर्णयानारब्धभेद ॱॱ न६४ भवति ३ ।      ॰ never entered, or an exit it did not record

॰ ══════════════════ the stages, in order ══════════════════
॰
॰ Each answers ० for "this stage refused", so a caller stops at the first
॰ refusal rather than carrying a half-built program forward. `chain.rs` returns
॰ `Result<_, String>` and maps each stage's own diagnostic into it; the
॰ diagnostics live in module state here and a reader asks the module that
॰ refused, which is the same information without the marshalling.

॰ ॥ पठनम् ॥ source octets to declarations — lex and parse.
सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः पठनम् आदाय मूल ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ ददाति न६४ आदि
    ॰ R-15-1 BEFORE ANYTHING IS TOKENISED, through the ONE gated source entry
    ॰ (W-304): `परिधिपदविभाग` resets and sets `परिधिदोषस्थितम्`/`परिधिदोषस्थानम्`
    ॰ and answers ० tokens on a refusal, which the test just below already stops on.
    ॰ W-342 — THE PARSER'S COUNT IS RESET HERE, BEFORE THE GATE, AND NOT ONLY
    ॰ WHERE THE PARSER RESETS IT. `कार्यक्रमपठनम्` zeroes `दोषसूचकाङ्क` on entry,
    ॰ and the return just below leaves before it is called. Measured: a
    ॰ comment-only source read right after a parse refusal still showed the
    ॰ refusal's १. `मण्डलसङ्कलनम्` asks this count, so without this line it
    ॰ would call the NEXT zero-token source — `lib.t1` — a parse refusal.
    व्याकरॱदोषसूचकाङ्क भवति ० ।
    चरः चिह्नकाः ॱॱ न६४ भवति अक्षरकोशॱपरिधिपदविभाग मूल ।
    यदि चिह्नकाः समम् ० आदि
        प्रत्यागमनम् ० ।
    इति
    चरः घोषणाः ॱॱ न६४ भवति व्याकरॱकार्यक्रमपठनम् चिह्नकाः ।
    ॰ ॥ FILL THE SHARED DECLARATION STORE ॥ `सङ्ग्रहः` copies this program out of
    ॰ `व्याकर`'s arena into `घोषणासञ्चय`, so a later source can name this one.
    ॰
    ॰ THIS DRIVER WAS BEHIND THE RUST ONE AND A TWIN TEST CAUGHT IT.
    ॰ `chain.rs`'s `Front::parse` has called this since the gather landed there;
    ॰ this routine did not, so the two drivers of one product diverged. The
    ॰ divergence surfaced as `the_t1_name_table_equals_the_rust_one_for_lex`
    ॰ failing on SYMBOL IDS and not on names: `कार्यक्रमनिर्णयः` calls
    ॰ `सञ्चयप्रकारबन्धः`, which is guarded by `सञ्चयसिद्धमस्ति` and MINTS a symbol
    ॰ per store entry before its own walk — so a driver that gathers numbers
    ॰ `lex`'s routines differently from one that does not.
    ॰
    ॰ THE FIX BELONGS HERE AND NOT IN THE TEST. Comparing the two tables by NAME
    ॰ would have passed today and hidden that the product's own driver was behind
    ॰ the scaffolding. The `.t1` half is the product; it must do everything the
    ॰ Rust driver does.
    चरः सङ्गृहीतम् ॱॱ न६४ भवति घोषणासञ्चयॱसङ्ग्रहः ।
    प्रत्यागमनम् घोषणाः ।
इति

॰ ॥ निर्णयः ॥ declarations to a resolved program — resolve, then typecheck.
॰
॰ TWO STAGES AND ONE ANSWER, because a caller can do nothing with a program
॰ that resolved and failed to typecheck: `मध्यरूप` would build IR against types
॰ `प्रकारपरीक्षा` refused. `chain.rs` keeps them separate because its caller is
॰ `t1_build`, which prints a stage name per refusal; the stage that refused is
॰ readable from the module here without threading it through a return —
॰ `निर्णयविरामभेद`, above, and that is now a global a reader can ask rather
॰ than a claim this margin made and nothing kept.
सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः निर्णयः आदाय घोषणाः ॱॱ न६४ ददाति बूल आदि
    ॰ RESET FIRST, so a reader of a SECOND call never sees the first's exit.
    निर्णयविरामभेद भवति निर्णयानारब्धभेद ।
    चरः निर्णायकः ॱॱ अर्थॱनिर्णायक भवति अर्थॱनिर्णायकारम्भः ।
    ॰ KEPT, NOT DROPPED. `परिसराः` is a FIELD of a `निर्णायक` and there may be
    ॰ many, so the resolver that RESOLVED THIS PROGRAM is the only one whose
    ॰ scopes name this program's routines. Building it as a local and letting it
    ॰ go is what left `नामसञ्चयः` with nothing but the placeholder symbol.
    निर्णायकधारः भवति निर्णायकः ।
    निर्णायकसिद्धः भवति सत्यम् ।
    ॰ ॥ LET THE RESOLVER CONSULT THE STORE ॥ Without this the gather above is
    ॰ wasted: the store is full and `कार्यक्रमनिर्णयः` does not read it.
    ॰
    ॰ AFTER `निर्णायकारम्भः` AND BEFORE `कार्यक्रमनिर्णयः`, which is where
    ॰ `chain.rs`'s `Front::resolve` puts it. `artha.t1` records that
    ॰ `सञ्चयसिद्धमस्ति` is NOT cleared by `निर्णायकारम्भः` and has no lowering
    ॰ routine, so the flag is one-way and calling it on every resolve is
    ॰ idempotent rather than careless.
    चरः सञ्चयसिद्धम् ॱॱ न६४ भवति अर्थॱसञ्चयसिद्धिः ।
    चरः निर्णीतम् ॱॱ बूल भवति अर्थॱकार्यक्रमनिर्णयः निर्णायकः घोषणाः ।
    यदि निर्णीतम् समम् असत्यम् आदि
        निर्णयविरामभेद भवति निर्णयनिर्णायकभेद ।
        प्रत्यागमनम् असत्यम् ।
    इति
    चरः परीक्षकः ॱॱ अर्थॱनिर्णायक भवति अर्थॱप्रकारपरीक्षकारम्भः निर्णायकः ।
    ॰ BOUND, NOT RETURNED DIRECTLY. The tail call answered `बूल` and the two
    ॰ refusals left the same one; binding it costs nothing and is what lets the
    ॰ typecheck refusal be written down separately from the resolve refusal.
    ॰ The answer this routine gives its callers is UNCHANGED.
    चरः परीक्षितम् ॱॱ बूल भवति अर्थॱकार्यक्रमप्रकारपरीक्षा घोषणाः ।
    यदि परीक्षितम् समम् असत्यम् आदि
        निर्णयविरामभेद भवति निर्णयप्रकारभेद ।
        प्रत्यागमनम् असत्यम् ।
    इति
    निर्णयविरामभेद भवति निर्णयसिद्धभेद ।
    प्रत्यागमनम् सत्यम् ।
इति

॰ ॥ रचना ॥ a resolved program to IR — how many routines were built.
सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः रचना आदाय घोषणाः ॱॱ न६४ ददाति न६४ आदि
    चरः रिक्तम् ॱॱ न६४ भवति मध्यरूपॱआरम्भः ।
    प्रत्यागमनम् मध्यरूपॱकार्यक्रमरचना घोषणाः ।
इति

॰ ॥ नामसञ्चयः ॥ fill the emitter's name table from the IR and the resolver.
॰
॰ THIS IS THE ONE STAGE THAT IS NOT A CALL, and it is what `chain.rs`'s bridge
॰ does from the other side: `paradigm_encode`'s `write_names_into_t1` walks
॰ `module.names` and calls `यन्त्रनामयोजनम्` per routine. The `.t1` side has the
॰ same data in four hops and no marshalling:
॰
॰   वृत्ति ॱ नाम             the routine's SymbolId
॰   अर्थॱसंज्ञाघोषणाकोश      symbol + १  ->  the declaration index
॰   घोषणा ॱ नामसूचकाङ्क       ->  the name's TOKEN index
॰   पदविभागॱचिह्नकपाठः        ->  its text
॰
॰ THE EMITTER REFUSES AN INCOMPLETE TABLE, which is what makes this loop
॰ verifiable rather than merely written: `यन्त्रमण्डलोत्सर्जनम्` answers an empty
॰ run when `यन्त्रचिह्नपरीक्षा` cannot name a routine. Fill it wrong and nothing
॰ is emitted — not something subtly wrong.
सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः नामसञ्चयः आदाय मण्डलनाम ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ ददाति न६४ आदि
    चरः रिक्तम् ॱॱ न६४ भवति यन्त्रोत्सर्जनॱयन्त्रनामारम्भः ।
    चरः नामसंख्या ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।
    चरः क्रमः ॱॱ न६४ भवति १ ।
    यावत् क्रमः न्यूनम् आरभ्य मध्यरूपॱवृत्तिसूचकाङ्क योगः १ समाप्तम् आदि
        चरः कार्यम् ॱॱ मध्यरूपॱवृत्ति भवति मध्यरूपॱवृत्तिकोश अङ्कः क्रमः अन्तः ।

        ॰ ══ THE SYMBOL, ASSIGNED HERE — `chain.rs:594-598` ══
        ॰
        ॰ `कार्यम् ॱ नाम` IS ० FOR EVERY ROUTINE on a `.t1`-only run, so the four
        ॰ hops below all read slot १ and every routine got the label of the
        ॰ file's FIRST DECLARATION. Fifteen routines, one name, and the emitter
        ॰ refused with LabelCollision — loudly, exactly as this routine's margin
        ॰ promised, rather than emitting fifteen identical labels into an object
        ॰ that would have linked and gone somewhere else.
        ॰
        ॰ THE NAME COMES FROM THE SIDE TABLE AND THE SYMBOL FROM THE RESOLVER,
        ॰ and it must be both. `वृत्तिनामचिह्नककोश` (`W-237`, by routine index)
        ॰ gives the declaration's name token directly — hop ३ without hops १
        ॰ and २. But the emitter's table is KEYED by symbol and so is every
        ॰ call: `यन्त्राह्वानोत्सर्जनम्` looks up `आह्वेयसंज्ञा`, which
        ॰ `ir.t1:1152` takes from the RESOLVER. Keying by routine index would
        ॰ give fifteen distinct labels and break every call in the corpus.
        चरः नामचिह्नकाङ्कः ॱॱ न६४ भवति मध्यरूपॱवृत्तिनामचिह्नककोश अङ्कः क्रमः अन्तः ।
        ॰ Token ० is the module's synthesised growth routine (ir.t1's वृद्धिवृत्तिसंज्ञा):
        ॰ its symbol is already in कार्यम् ॱ नाम; name it (module, "खण्डवृद्धिः").
        ॰ `V-009` (ii): token ० is also one of the two matrix kernel routines,
        ॰ told apart by the symbol `ir.t1` gave them: (module, "आव्यूहगुणनम्") and
        ॰ (module, "व्युत्क्रमः") — `chain.rs`'s twin reads the same symbols.
        यदि नामचिह्नकाङ्कः समम् ० आदि
            चरः संश्लिष्टनाम ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति उक्तम् खण्डवृद्धिः इति ।
            यदि कार्यम् ॱ नाम समम् मध्यरूपॱआव्यूहवृत्तिसंज्ञा आदि
                संश्लिष्टनाम भवति उक्तम् आव्यूहगुणनम् इति ।
            इति
            यदि कार्यम् ॱ नाम समम् मध्यरूपॱव्युत्क्रमवृत्तिसंज्ञा आदि
                संश्लिष्टनाम भवति उक्तम् व्युत्क्रमः इति ।
            इति
            ॰ FORK-JOIN: the region marker routine (ir.t1's समान्तरवृत्तिसंज्ञा), named
            ॰ (module, "समाप्तम्"). A KEYWORD, so that no routine a program declares can
            ॰ have its label (review D: a user routine named `समान्तरचालनम्`, the
            ॰ first spelling, refused the build with LabelCollision). A declared name is
            ॰ an identifier, and the reader prefers the keyword, so `वृत्तिः समाप्तम्`
            ॰ never declares a routine; the runtime finds the marker by its first word.
            ॰ MEASURED OTHERWISE 2026-10-10 (0b45b5f5): `वृत्तिपठनम्` takes ANY token as a
            ॰ routine's name, so `वृत्तिः समाप्तम्` beside a region (and `वृत्तिः खण्डवृद्धिः`
            ॰ beside a growing run) reached the emitter's LabelCollision, and `वृत्तिः अन्यथा`
            ॰ builds. No label can be made safe here: the label is written into T0 text as
            ॰ ONE akṣara word, which is exactly what a T1 name is (a label with a space broke
            ॰ the link). So these six names are RESERVED where the build synthesises them:
            ॰ `मध्यरूपॱसंश्लिष्टनामपरीक्षा` refuses a routine that declares one (संश्लिष्टनामनिषेधः,
            ॰ 0x382) before the emitter is reached. Its spellings must stay these six.
            यदि कार्यम् ॱ नाम समम् मध्यरूपॱसमान्तरवृत्तिसंज्ञा आदि
                संश्लिष्टनाम भवति उक्तम् समाप्तम् इति ।
            इति
            ॰ ARENAS: the module's arena routine (ir.t1's वाटवृत्तिसंज्ञा), named with another
            ॰ KEYWORD for the same reason, (module, "अन्यथा").
            यदि कार्यम् ॱ नाम समम् मध्यरूपॱवाटवृत्तिसंज्ञा आदि
                संश्लिष्टनाम भवति उक्तम् अन्यथा इति ।
            इति
            ॰ `N-004`: the module's run compare (ir.t1's साम्यवृत्तिसंज्ञा).
            यदि कार्यम् ॱ नाम समम् मध्यरूपॱसाम्यवृत्तिसंज्ञा आदि
                संश्लिष्टनाम भवति उक्तम् खण्डसाम्यम् इति ।
            इति
            चरः वृद्धिस्थलम् ॱॱ न६४ भवति यन्त्रोत्सर्जनॱयन्त्रनामयोजनम् आरभ्य कार्यम् ॱ नाम ऽ मण्डलनाम ऽ संश्लिष्टनाम समाप्तम् ।
            नामसंख्या भवति नामसंख्या योगः १ ।
        इति अन्यथा आदि
        चरः नामचिह्नकम् ॱॱ पदविभागॱचिह्नक भवति पदविभागॱचिह्नककोश अङ्कः नामचिह्नकाङ्कः अन्तः ।
        चरः वृत्तिनाम ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति पदविभागॱचिह्नकपाठः नामचिह्नकम् ।

        ॰ `अर्थॱनामनिर्णयः`, NOT A LOOKUP OF OUR OWN. The first version of this
        ॰ walked `परिसराः` here — twenty-five lines that duplicated
        ॰ `artha.t1:443` and reproduced a bug it had already fixed. Its margin
        ॰ at `:447` names the trap exactly: *"`अधिकम् १` AND NOT `अधिकम् ०`: the
        ॰ walk stops ABOVE the reserved slot. With ० it ran one iteration too
        ॰ far and asked slot ० for its `प्रविष्टयः`"* — which is the fault this
        ॰ file raised, verbatim, on its first run.
        ॰
        ॰ AND THE SECOND HALF OF THAT MARGIN IS WHY THE DUPLICATE WAS DANGEROUS
        ॰ RATHER THAN MERELY REDUNDANT: *"a name it DOES carry answered only
        ॰ because it returned first."* The reserved-slot read is reached only
        ॰ when the name is ABSENT, so a copy of this walk passes every test whose
        ॰ names all resolve and faults on the first that does not.
        ॰
        ॰ It also walks OUTERMOST-FIRST by construction, which `:440` says is
        ॰ load-bearing: the other direction "finds the GLOBAL that a parameter
        ॰ shadows, so a function would silently read the wrong variable while
        ॰ resolving cleanly". A hand-written scan gets that right by luck.
        चरः निर्णीता ॱॱ सम्भाव्य न६४ भवति अर्थॱनामनिर्णयः निर्णायकधारः वृत्तिनाम ।
        चरः संज्ञा ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।
        ॰ `+१` MIRRORS `chain.rs:550`'s `int_of(e, "संज्ञा") + 1`: the entry
        ॰ holds the bare SymbolId and `संज्ञाभेदकोश` and `संज्ञाघोषणाकोश` are
        ॰ both keyed by symbol PLUS ONE.
        यदि निर्णीता असमम् शून्यम् आदि
            संज्ञा भवति आरभ्य निर्णीता योगः १ समाप्तम् ।
        इति
        ॰ THE KIND CHECK IS NOT DECORATION: a name may resolve to a symbol that
        ॰ is not a routine — `पदभेद` is a `सार्वजनिक चरः` and would answer here.
        यदि संज्ञा अधिकम् ० आदि
            यदि अर्थॱसंज्ञाभेदकोश अङ्कः संज्ञा अन्तः असमम् व्याकरॱवृत्तिघोषणाभेद आदि
                संज्ञा भवति ० ।
            इति
        इति
        ॰ A ROUTINE THE RESOLVER DID NOT NAME IS NUMBERED APART so it cannot
        ॰ collide with a symbol the resolver minted — `chain.rs:597`'s own
        ॰ reason, and the fallback is what keeps a nameless routine from
        ॰ colliding with every other nameless one at ०.
        यदि संज्ञा समम् ० आदि
            संज्ञा भवति आरभ्य १०००००० योगः क्रमः समाप्तम् ।
        इति
        ॰ WRITTEN BACK WHERE THE EMITTER READS IT — the `.t1` twin of
        ॰ `chain.rs:616`. Records are shared by reference, so this fills the
        ॰ arena entry `यन्त्रचिह्नपरीक्षा` and every call will look up.
        कार्यम् ॱ नाम भवति संज्ञा ।
        ॰ ० IS A VALID SymbolId HERE AND GUARDING AGAINST IT REJECTED THE ONLY
        ॰ ROUTINE. The `+१` that makes ० mean "none" lives in the ARENA INDEX —
        ॰ `संज्ञाघोषणाकोश` is keyed by `symbol + १`, so symbol ० reads slot १ —
        ॰ and `वृत्ति ॱ नाम` holds the bare SymbolId. A first-written guard
        ॰ `यदि संज्ञा अधिकम् ०` recorded zero names for a single-routine module
        ॰ and would have looked like an empty program rather than a wrong loop.
        ॰ The absence test belongs on the INDEXED value, which is below.
        ॰
        ॰ HOPS १ AND २ ARE GONE. They existed only to reach the declaration's
        ॰ name token, and `वृत्तिनामचिह्नककोश` holds that directly, by the same
        ॰ routine index this loop already walks. The long way round was the only
        ॰ way that could be wrong: it routed through `वृत्ति ॱ नाम`, which is
        ॰ ० until something assigns it.
        यदि वृत्तिनाम ॱ दैर्घ्य अधिकम् ० आदि
            चरः स्थलम् ॱॱ न६४ भवति यन्त्रोत्सर्जनॱयन्त्रनामयोजनम् आरभ्य संज्ञा ऽ मण्डलनाम ऽ वृत्तिनाम समाप्तम् ।
            नामसंख्या भवति नामसंख्या योगः १ ।
        इति
        इति
        क्रमः भवति क्रमः योगः १ ।
    इति
    ॰ AND THE GLOBALS, WHICH THE LOOP ABOVE CANNOT REACH AT ALL. It walks
    ॰ `मध्यरूपॱवृत्तिसूचकाङ्क` — routines — and on `ashtaka.t1` that is nine of
    ॰ fifteen symbols. The module takes ०, the six globals take १-६ and the nine
    ॰ routines ७-१५, measured, so the six were not a hole in the table but a
    ॰ POPULATION THE WALK NEVER COVERED. The emitter refused symbol ४,
    ॰ `अष्टकदोषमस्ति`, which is the fourth of them.
    ॰ WHY THIS WAS INVISIBLE: a module whose globals are never relocated against
    ॰ emits correctly with all six missing, so the defect is silent in exactly
    ॰ the modules a small fixture is made of. The four-line toy in `t1_driver.rs`
    ॰ has no globals and passes without this loop.
    ॰ THE RESOLVER IS THE ONLY WAY ACROSS: `वैश्विकमण्डलकोश`, `वैश्विकनामकोश` and
    ॰ `वैश्विकमूल्यकोश` (`ir.t1:422-428`) carry the module, the name and the value
    ॰ and NO symbol field, so the name must be resolved rather than read.
    ॰ १-BASED AND CURSOR-COUNTED like the appender arenas: `ir.t1:2054` advances
    ॰ `वैश्विकसञ्चयसूचकाङ्क` BEFORE it writes, so slot ० is never filled and the
    ॰ walk runs १..सूचकाङ्क. It is not the `परिसराः` convention, where ० is
    ॰ reserved with `शून्यम्` and a walk must stop above it.
    चरः वैक्रमः ॱॱ न६४ भवति १ ।
    यावत् वैक्रमः न्यूनम् आरभ्य मध्यरूपॱवैश्विकसञ्चयसूचकाङ्क योगः १ समाप्तम् आदि
        चरः वैनाम ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति मध्यरूपॱवैश्विकनामकोश अङ्कः वैक्रमः अन्तः ।
        चरः वैमण्डल ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति मध्यरूपॱवैश्विकमण्डलकोश अङ्कः वैक्रमः अन्तः ।
        यदि वैनाम ॱ दैर्घ्य अधिकम् ० आदि
            चरः वैनिर्णीता ॱॱ सम्भाव्य न६४ भवति अर्थॱनामनिर्णयः निर्णायकधारः वैनाम ।
            यदि वैनिर्णीता असमम् शून्यम् आदि
                ॰ THE SAME EXPRESSION THE ROUTINE PASS USES, deliberately: the two
                ॰ populations share one symbol space, so a different arithmetic
                ॰ here would key the globals into a space of its own. The routine
                ॰ half of it is confirmed by measurement — ७-१५ against declaration
                ॰ indices ७-१५ — and the falsifier for this half is that the six
                ॰ land on १-६ and the table comes back contiguous १-१५.
                चरः वैसंज्ञा ॱॱ न६४ भवति आरभ्य वैनिर्णीता योगः १ समाप्तम् ।
                चरः वैस्थलम् ॱॱ न६४ भवति यन्त्रोत्सर्जनॱयन्त्रनामयोजनम् आरभ्य वैसंज्ञा ऽ वैमण्डल ऽ वैनाम समाप्तम् ।
                नामसंख्या भवति नामसंख्या योगः १ ।
            इति
        इति
        वैक्रमः भवति वैक्रमः योगः १ ।
    इति
    ॰ THE LOWERING HALF OF वास्तु, 2026-09-13: a cross-module global READ now lowers
    ॰ to वैश्विकाज्ञाभेद carrying the resolver's symbol (ir.t1's cause-44 arm asks
    ॰ the checker for the type first). The emitter turns that symbol into a label
    ॰ only if the symbol is NAMED — and the two loops above name only this
    ॰ module's routines and globals. The resolver mints one symbol per registry
    ॰ entry it resolves (`अर्थॱसञ्चयसंज्ञाप्रविष्टयः` beside `अर्थॱसञ्चयसंज्ञामूल्यानि`),
    ॰ so every registry-resolved GLOBAL symbol is registered here as (declaring
    ॰ module, member): the label is the one the data-only object exports.
    चरः सञ्चितक्रमः ॱॱ न६४ भवति १ ।
    यावत् सञ्चितक्रमः न्यूनम् आरभ्य अर्थॱसञ्चयसंज्ञासूचकाङ्क योगः १ समाप्तम् आदि
        चरः सञ्चितप्रविष्टिः ॱॱ न६४ भवति अर्थॱसञ्चयसंज्ञाप्रविष्टयः अङ्कः सञ्चितक्रमः अन्तः ।
        चरः सञ्चितसंज्ञा ॱॱ न६४ भवति अर्थॱसञ्चयसंज्ञामूल्यानि अङ्कः सञ्चितक्रमः अन्तः ।
        यदि सञ्चितप्रविष्टिः अधिकम् ० आदि
            ॰ EVERY registry-resolved symbol, routines included (2026-09-13): a
            ॰ cross-module CALLEE is a symbol the emitter must name too, and under
            ॰ the census the Rust twin had always named it — so the product path
            ॰ refused every module with imports at emit (UnnamedSymbol) on its own.
            ॰ The label is module ⧺ member for routines and globals alike.
            यदि सञ्चितसंज्ञा अधिकम् ० आदि
                चरः सञ्चितमण्डलम् ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति घोषणासञ्चयॱमण्डलनाम आरभ्य घोषणासञ्चयॱप्रविष्टिमण्डलम् सञ्चितप्रविष्टिः समाप्तम् ।
                चरः सञ्चितनाम ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति घोषणासञ्चयॱप्रविष्टिनाम सञ्चितप्रविष्टिः ।
                चरः सञ्चितस्थलम् ॱॱ न६४ भवति यन्त्रोत्सर्जनॱयन्त्रनामयोजनम् आरभ्य सञ्चितसंज्ञा ऽ सञ्चितमण्डलम् ऽ सञ्चितनाम समाप्तम् ।
                नामसंख्या भवति नामसंख्या योगः १ ।
            इति
        इति
        सञ्चितक्रमः भवति सञ्चितक्रमः योगः १ ।
    इति
    ॰ The record cursor the emitters own (module-less label): run growth bumps it.
    चरः रिक्तमण्डलनाम ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति पदविभागॱखण्डपाठः आरभ्य उक्तम् क इति ऽ ० ऽ ० समाप्तम् ।
    चरः सूचकस्थलम् ॱॱ न६४ भवति यन्त्रोत्सर्जनॱयन्त्रनामयोजनम् आरभ्य मध्यरूपॱरचनासूचकसंज्ञा ऽ रिक्तमण्डलनाम ऽ उक्तम् रचनासूचकः इति समाप्तम् ।
        चरः क्षेत्रस्थलम् ॱॱ न६४ भवति यन्त्रोत्सर्जनॱयन्त्रनामयोजनम् आरभ्य मध्यरूपॱरचनाक्षेत्रसंज्ञा ऽ रिक्तमण्डलनाम ऽ उक्तम् रचनाक्षेत्रम् इति समाप्तम् ।
    नामसंख्या भवति नामसंख्या योगः २ ।
    प्रत्यागमनम् नामसंख्या ।
इति

॰ ॥ उत्सर्जनम् ॥ the built IR to Sassembly text.
॰
॰ The last stage of the front half, and the join to the back one: what comes out
॰ is a Sassembly SOURCE, which `वाक्यविभागॱसङ्कलनम्` reads and `कोश` turns into an
॰ image. The two halves meet as TEXT, which is why the driver stops here.
सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः उत्सर्जनम् ददाति अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ आदि
    प्रत्यागमनम् यन्त्रोत्सर्जनॱयन्त्रमण्डलोत्सर्जनम् ।
इति

॰ ॥ सङ्कलनम् ॥ THE WHOLE FRONT HALF: a `.t1` source to Sassembly text.
॰
॰ `chain.rs`'s stage sequence, in the order it runs them, answering the empty
॰ run wherever a stage refuses — so a caller that gets octets got them from a
॰ program that lexed, parsed, resolved, typechecked, built IR and emitted.
सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः मण्डलसङ्कलनम् आदाय मूल ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ ऽ मण्डलनाम ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ ददाति अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ आदि
    ॰ RESET ON ENTRY, TO THE SENTINEL AND NOT TO SUCCESS. Without the reset a
    ॰ caller reading the global after a refusal could be reading the PREVIOUS
    ॰ call's exit — the stale-value failure that makes a recorded reason worse
    ॰ than none. Without the SENTINEL, a return that forgets to set the code
    ॰ reports "emitted", and this routine's whole history is returns that
    ॰ recorded nothing.
    सङ्कलनविरामभेद भवति सङ्कलनानारब्धभेद ।
    चरः रिक्तम् ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति ० ।
    चरः घोषणाः ॱॱ न६४ भवति पठनम् मूल ।
    यदि घोषणाः समम् ० आदि
        ॰ W-345 — TWO CAUSES BEHIND ONE ZERO. `पठनम्` answers ० both when the
        ॰ gate refused an octet outside R-15-1 and when the source parsed to no
        ॰ declarations; the gate's record is the discriminator, reset by
        ॰ `परिधिपदविभाग` on entry so it is never a previous source's verdict.
        ॰ W-342 — AND A THIRD. A source that lexed and that the PARSER refused
        ॰ answers ० as well; `व्याकरॱदोषसूचकाङ्क` is its discriminator, zeroed
        ॰ by `पठनम्` before the gate so it too is never a previous source's.
        ॰ The gate is asked FIRST: a source it refused never reached the parser.
        यदि अक्षरकोशॱपरिधिदोषस्थितम् समम् सत्यम् आदि
            सङ्कलनविरामभेद भवति सङ्कलनपरिधिभेद ।
        इति अन्यथा आदि
            यदि व्याकरॱदोषसूचकाङ्क अधिकम् ० आदि
                सङ्कलनविरामभेद भवति सङ्कलनव्याकरणभेद ।
            इति अन्यथा आदि
                सङ्कलनविरामभेद भवति सङ्कलनाघोषणाभेद ।
            इति
        इति
        प्रत्यागमनम् रिक्तम् ।
    इति
    यदि निर्णयः घोषणाः समम् असत्यम् आदि
        सङ्कलनविरामभेद भवति सङ्कलनानिर्णयभेद ।
        प्रत्यागमनम् रिक्तम् ।
    इति
    चरः वृत्तयः ॱॱ न६४ भवति रचना घोषणाः ।
    यदि मध्यरूपॱप्राचलरक्षादोषसंख्या अधिकम् ० आदि
        सङ्कलनविरामभेद भवति सङ्कलनप्राचलरक्षाभेद ।
        प्रत्यागमनम् रिक्तम् ।
    इति
    ॰ `V-005`: a value crossing into a declared file it is not in refused the
    ॰ program in `मध्यरूप` (`FileMismatch`); `chain.rs`'s `refusal_site` names it.
    यदि मध्यरूपॱवर्गविरोधमस्ति समम् सत्यम् आदि
        सङ्कलनविरामभेद भवति सङ्कलनवर्गविरोधभेद ।
        प्रत्यागमनम् रिक्तम् ।
    इति
    ॰ THE ROUTINE GUARD IS GONE, AND IT WAS NEVER A PROTECTION. Its own margin
    ॰ said so when W-280 landed it: *NOT AN ERROR: a module of pure data reaches
    ॰ here. It is still an early return, because emitting a routine-less module
    ॰ is a SECOND capability.* **It deferred a capability; it did not guard a
    ॰ defect.** Compare `पाठवस्तुरचना`'s instruction guard, whose margin records a
    ॰ failure that was once live — those are different kinds of sentence and only
    ॰ one of them needs a replacement before it can be removed.
    ॰
    ॰ MEASURED BEFORE REMOVING, stage by stage, past the guard:
    ॰   ast.t1    decls 48 · routines ० · नामानि 45 · ir globals 45
    ॰   vastu.t1  decls 12 · routines ० · नामानि  6 · ir globals  6
    ॰ Both files of `वास्तु` have ZERO routines and NON-ZERO names, so
    ॰ `यदि नामानि समम् ०` below still answers for a module that truly declares
    ॰ nothing. `सङ्कलनावृत्तिभेद` stays declared and is now unreachable — named
    ॰ as such rather than deleted, because its absence is the record that a
    ॰ routine-less module used to be refused here.
    ॰
    ॰
    ॰ AND `vastu.t1` IS NOT THE EMPTY CASE I PREDICTED. I registered it as ० and
    ॰ ०; it has 6 IR globals, because a `संरचना` and a `गणना` each become one.
    ॰ Types are not nothing to the lowering.
    ॰ THE CURSOR BEFORE AND AFTER, BECAUSE THE APPENDER IS AN UPSERT.
    ॰ `यन्त्रनामयोजनम्` (`yantrotsarjana.t1:181-200`) scans for the key first and
    ॰ advances `यन्त्रनामसूचकाङ्क` only when it finds none, so N calls carrying
    ॰ one repeated symbol leave ONE entry. `नामानि` counts the CALLS.
    ॰ **THE ABSOLUTE CURSOR, BECAUSE THE RESET IS INSIDE THIS WINDOW.** The margin
    ॰ here used to argue the opposite — "a delta is right whether or not the table
    ॰ is reset between the sources of one corpus walk" — and that is the wrong
    ॰ boundary. A delta survives a reset BETWEEN sources; it is destroyed by one
    ॰ INSIDE the interval it measures, and `नामसञ्चयः` opens by calling
    ॰ `यन्त्रोत्सर्जनॱयन्त्रनामारम्भः` (`:239` → `yantrotsarjana.t1:165`), which
    ॰ zeroes the cursor. So the cursor AFTER the call is already this call's count.
    ॰
    ॰ MEASURED, AND THE OLD FORM RETURNED AN IMPOSSIBLE NUMBER:
    ॰   ashtaka.t1  before ०  after १५  delta १५ — right BY ACCIDENT, it ran first
    ॰   ast.t1      before १५ after ४५  delta ३० — 45 of 45 were named
    ॰   vastu.t1    before ४५ after ६   delta −३९ — NEGATIVE, 6 of 6 were named
    ॰ A count of entries written cannot be negative, and `असमम्` accepted it
    ॰ without complaint. Both data-only modules were refused while correct; the
    ॰ control passed only because `before` was ० for the FIRST source, which is
    ॰ why a whole-corpus walk was exposed for sources 2..N and not just for `वास्तु`.
    ॰
    ॰ **THE NAME TABLE ITSELF WAS NEVER CONTAMINATED — GUARD BUG, NOT ARTEFACT
    ॰ BUG — AND THE WITNESS IS `ast.t1`'s ४५, NOT ६०.** The obvious next question
    ॰ is whether the walk also produced wrong IMAGES for sources 2..N. It did not,
    ॰ and the three rows above already settle it without another run: had the
    ॰ table accumulated across sources, `ast`'s `after` would be ६० — ashtaka's १५
    ॰ carried plus its own ४५ — and `vastu`'s would be ५१. They are ४५ and ६, each
    ॰ equal to that source's TRUE count, and that equality holds for the two
    ॰ sources whose `before` was non-zero. Only a reset inside every window
    ॰ produces that. A table that had really accumulated could not yield −३९ at
    ॰ all. Reading the absolute is therefore not a workaround for a dirty table;
    ॰ it is the only correct reading OF A CLEAN ONE, and the reset-on-entry is
    ॰ exactly what makes it correct.
    ॰
    ॰ AND THE CLAIM IS STRONGER THAN "THE DELTA WAS WRONG": the reset is on entry,
    ॰ so the post-call cursor IS this call's count. **THERE WAS NO DELTA TO TAKE.**
    ॰ The subtraction was not an equivalent formulation that happened to fail — it
    ॰ was strictly worse than the raw reading it was computed from.
    ॰
    ॰ SCOPE OF THAT RULING — IT IS THE NAME ARENA ALONE. `यन्त्राधिकरणसीमा` and
    ॰ `यन्त्रनिक्षेपाः` (`yantrotsarjana.t1:581-582`) carry their own cursors under
    ॰ their own reset discipline, and nothing measured here speaks to them. The
    ॰ unit's arena assertion is the control for whether reset-on-entry is
    ॰ universal or belongs to the name table only: if either moves across a
    ॰ `वास्तु` emit, the same defect is present in an arena where it would NOT go
    ॰ negative and would read as a plausible partial loss.
    चरः नामानि ॱॱ न६४ भवति नामसञ्चयः मण्डलनाम ।
    चरः प्रविष्टयः ॱॱ न६४ भवति यन्त्रोत्सर्जनॱयन्त्रनामसूचकाङ्क ।
    ॰ RECORDED BEFORE THE GUARD, so both are readable on the REFUSING path too —
    ॰ a diagnostic written only on the success path answers only where it is not
    ॰ needed.
    सङ्कलननामप्रयासाः भवति नामानि ।
    सङ्कलननामप्रविष्टयः भवति प्रविष्टयः ।
    ॰ A ZERO-CHECK CANNOT SEE THE DEFECT MEASURED ON `lex.t1`: fifteen routines
    ॰ walked, fifteen insertions attempted, ONE entry — `नामानि` answers १५ and
    ॰ `समम् ०` is satisfied. Every interesting failure here is NON-ZERO, so the
    ॰ question is not whether anything was written but whether each attempt
    ॰ became its OWN entry.
    ॰ THE DELTA AND NOT THE CURSOR: a delta is right whether or not the table is
    ॰ reset between the sources of one corpus walk; the absolute cursor is right
    ॰ only if it is, and that is a property of another module's reset order.
    ॰ AGAINST `नामानि` AND NOT `वृत्तयः`, deliberately: the two are the same
    ॰ number today, but `वृत्तयः` counts what `रचना` lowered while `नामानि`
    ॰ counts what THIS pass attempted, and a routine skipped for an empty name
    ॰ would make a `वृत्तयः` comparison refuse a module over a difference this
    ॰ guard is not about.
    ॰ **A SIGN GUARD WAS WRITTEN HERE AND REMOVED BEFORE LANDING, DELIBERATELY.**
    ॰ The −३९ was impossible, not merely wrong, and nothing refused it — which
    ॰ argues for a guard that rejects a negative COUNT with its own exit. It was
    ॰ implemented, then withdrawn, because its premise expired in this same diff:
    ॰ `प्रविष्टयः` is now an absolute cursor, and a cursor cannot go negative by
    ॰ the mechanism that produced −३९. That value existed ONLY because a
    ॰ subtraction spanned a reset, and the subtraction is gone.
    ॰
    ॰ Shipping it would have contradicted this unit's own thesis inside its own
    ॰ diff: an exit whose premise has gone is exactly how `सङ्कलनावृत्तिभेद` came
    ॰ to sit declared at in-degree ०, which this commit repairs. A margin does not
    ॰ rescue such an exit — `सङ्कलनावृत्तिभेद` HAD an honest margin and was still
    ॰ wrong to be there.
    ॰
    ॰ AND THE COST WAS MEASURED, NOT HYPOTHETICAL: the first draft gave it the
    ॰ value ६, which `सङ्कलनानारब्धभेद` — the sentinel — already holds. A broken
    ॰ count would have reported as "no exit was recorded": two conditions sharing
    ॰ one code, the precise fault this family of exits exists to prevent.
    ॰
    ॰ THE `असमम्` BELOW IS WHERE A REAL CORRUPTION SURFACES. A candidate remains,
    ॰ unswept and owned by nobody yet: sign assertions across the arena cursors
    ॰ (`यन्त्राधिकरणसीमा`, `यन्त्रनिक्षेपाः`, `यन्त्रप्रवेशसंज्ञा`), where deltas
    ॰ are still taken and a negative IS reachable.
    यदि प्रविष्टयः असमम् नामानि आदि
        सङ्कलनविरामभेद भवति सङ्कलननामवैषम्यभेद ।
        प्रत्यागमनम् रिक्तम् ।
    इति
    यदि नामानि समम् ० आदि
        सङ्कलनविरामभेद भवति सङ्कलनानामभेद ।
        प्रत्यागमनम् रिक्तम् ।
    इति
    ॰ ══ THE SUCCESS EXIT EXAMINED WHAT IT RETURNS, WHICH IT NEVER DID ══
    ॰
    ॰ Both guards above test the NAME TABLE. Neither tested the ARTEFACT, so this
    ॰ routine validated its intermediate state, declared `सिद्ध`, and handed back
    ॰ `उत्सर्जनम्` unexamined. Measured 2026-09-15: TEN of the twenty corpus
    ॰ sources — `81.7%` of the corpus by routine count, `encode` 138 routines,
    ॰ `shrinkhala` 99 — left here with ZERO octets and the code that means
    ॰ EMITTED. The hop ladder read the empty run, scored `Hops(0)`, and the census
    ॰ counted ten sources that "did not emit" while this routine said they had.
    ॰
    ॰ THE SIGN IS WHAT MAKES IT WORSE THAN `१००३`. That was a false REFUSAL: loud,
    ॰ pipeline-stopping, and therefore eventually investigated. This is a false
    ॰ SUCCESS — it hands an empty artefact downstream and every later stage
    ॰ behaves as though there were nothing to do.
    ॰
    ॰ `वृत्तयः` IS THE DISCRIMINATOR AND IT HAS BEEN IN SCOPE SINCE `:505`. An
    ॰ empty emission is LEGITIMATE for a module that built no routines — `ast.t1`
    ॰ and `vastu.t1` declare none and correctly reach the ladder's last rung. It
    ॰ is a CONTRADICTION for a module that built some. A shared representation for
    ॰ failure and success is a defect only where an empty success is legitimate,
    ॰ and this is the site where it is not.
    ॰
    ॰ NOT A FIX OF THE EMPTINESS. The emitter refuses upstream with
    ॰ `यन्त्रानामसंज्ञानिषेधभेद` (`Refusal::UnnamedSymbol`) and records its own
    ॰ variant and subject; that defect is open. This stops the lie about it.
    ॰ BOUND ONCE, NOT CALLED TWICE. `उत्सर्जनम्` is a routine and emits the whole
    ॰ module; testing it and then returning it would run the emitter twice.
    चरः निर्गमः ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति उत्सर्जनम् ।
    यदि वृत्तयः अधिकम् ० आदि
        यदि निर्गमः ॱ दैर्घ्य समम् ० आदि
            सङ्कलनविरामभेद भवति सङ्कलनानुत्सर्जनभेद ।
            प्रत्यागमनम् रिक्तम् ।
        इति
    इति
    सङ्कलनविरामभेद भवति सङ्कलनसिद्धभेद ।
    प्रत्यागमनम् निर्गमः ।
इति


॰ ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
॰ THE BACK HALF — `W-279`. Until this, `शृङ्खला` ended at
॰ `यन्त्रमण्डलोत्सर्जनम्` and every cross-module call in it was
॰ `यन्त्रोत्सर्जनॱ…`: the driver produced Sassembly TEXT and nothing more.
॰
॰ THE JOIN WAS ALREADY PROVEN AND THAT IS NOT THE SAME CLAIM. A test drove the
॰ emitter's text into `वाक्यविभागॱसङ्कलनम्` and out as instructions, in one
॰ test, with no Rust COMPILER stage between the halves — but RUST CALLED BOTH
॰ HALVES. The driver sat on one side of that join and never crossed it. The
॰ acceptance for this row is that `शृङ्खला` calls them, not that they can be
॰ called.
॰
॰ THE STAGES, AND EACH ONE ALREADY EXISTED:
॰   वाक्यविभागॱसङ्कलनम्      text     -> statements, आज्ञाकोश filled
॰   वाक्यविभागॱकार्यक्रमरचना  the arenas -> one कार्यक्रम
॰   सङ्केतनॱस्थानविन्यासः     कार्यक्रम  -> the layout, one address per instruction
॰   सङ्केतनॱवस्तुसङ्केतनम्    कार्यक्रम  -> the object's text octets
॰   सङ्केतनॱवस्तुरचना        the above -> a वास्तुॱवस्तु
॰   संयोजनॱसंयोजनम्          objects   -> a संयोजितम्
॰   कोशॱप्रतिबिम्बलेखनम्     that      -> an ELF image
॰
॰ NOTHING HERE IS NEW CODE IN ANOTHER MODULE. Every routine above was landed,
॰ tested and reachable; what did not exist was a `.t1` caller that ran them in
॰ order. THE ROW IS THE ORDERING.
॰ ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

॰ the assembler's tables, read once before any source is assembled.
॰ `आरम्भः` CLEARS the table cursors, so it must come FIRST and the two readers
॰ after it — reading first and resetting after empties them, which is a
॰ layout that assembles cleanly and branches to the wrong place.
सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः सङ्कलनारम्भः ददाति न६४ आदि
    चरः रिक्तम् ॱॱ अ६४ भवति वाक्यविभागॱआरम्भः ।
    ॰ THE STORE FIRST (2026-09-14). `संज्ञाकुलपठनम्` and its siblings read their table
    ॰ from `पदविभागॱसमावेशपाठः`, which answers from the store; interpreted the host fills
    ॰ it at load, natively nothing did, so this fills it from `सारणी` — a module generated
    ॰ from `spec/` by tools/mkspectables.py. Guarded inside, so a second call is a no-op.
    चरः सारण्यः ॱॱ न६४ भवति समावेशसारणीॱसारणीपूरणम् ।
    चरः कुलानि ॱॱ न६४ भवति वाक्यविभागॱसंज्ञाकुलपठनम् ।
    चरः निर्देशाः ॱॱ न६४ भवति वाक्यविभागॱनिर्देशकोशपठनम् ।
    प्रत्यागमनम् निर्देशाः ।
इति

॰ Sassembly text to a linkable object — the half `वस्तुरचना` made possible.
॰ शून्यम् wherever a stage refuses, and the stage's own diagnostic is left
॰ where that stage records it rather than copied here.
सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः पाठवस्तुरचना आदाय पाठ्यम् ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ ददाति सम्भाव्य वास्तुॱवस्तु आदि
    ॰ RESET ON ENTRY, TO THE SENTINEL AND NOT TO SUCCESS — the same reason as
    ॰ `सङ्कलनविरामभेद`: without the reset a caller reads the PREVIOUS call's exit,
    ॰ and without the sentinel a future return that forgets to record reports
    ॰ "built" to everyone.
    वस्तुरचनाविरामभेद भवति वस्तुरचनानारब्धभेद ।
    चरः वाक्यानि ॱॱ न६४ भवति वाक्यविभागॱसङ्कलनम् पाठ्यम् ।
    ॰ W-302: A RECORDED REFUSAL IS A REFUSAL. Rust's parse() returns Err when its
    ॰ error list is non-empty, and the whole file is refused. This read the
    ॰ statement count only, so a data directive in ॱपाठ — P28, recorded by the
    ॰ splitter and its statement skipped — built an object with that directive's
    ॰ octets missing and said nothing. Asked FIRST, before the count, because a
    ॰ file whose only statement was refused would otherwise read as "no
    ॰ statements" or "nothing built" and hide the cause the record names.
    यदि वाक्यविभागॱवाक्यविभागदोषसूचकाङ्क अधिकम् ० आदि
        वस्तुरचनाविरामभेद भवति वस्तुरचनावाक्यदोषभेद ।
        प्रत्यागमनम् शून्यम् ।
    इति
    यदि वाक्यानि समम् ० आदि
        वस्तुरचनाविरामभेद भवति वस्तुरचनावाक्यभेद ।
        प्रत्यागमनम् शून्यम् ।
    इति

    ॰ A SPLITTER WITH NO READER BEHIND IT ANSWERS A PLAUSIBLE NUMBER AND BUILDS
    ॰ NOTHING, which is what `सङ्कलनम्` did before the sentence reader was
    ॰ joined to it. So the instruction count is asked for, not assumed.
    ॰
    ॰ **NARROWED, NOT REMOVED — AND THE DEFECT AND THE LEGITIMATE CASE SHARE A
    ॰ SIGNATURE ON THE INSTRUCTION COUNT ALONE.** A module of pure data also
    ॰ answers `वाक्यानि > ०` with `आज्ञासूचकाङ्क == ०`. Asking only about
    ॰ instructions cannot tell the two apart, so this asks whether ANYTHING was
    ॰ built.
    ॰
    ॰ **THE MODULE NAME IS NOT THE FILE.** An earlier draft of this margin said
    ॰ "that is `वास्तु`, 45 globals" — but TWO files declare module `वास्तु`, and
    ॰ 45 is `ast.t1`'s count, not `vastu.t1`'s. Measured per file:
    ॰   ast.t1    49 declarations · 45 globals · 0 routines
    ॰   vastu.t1   7 declarations ·  6 globals · 0 routines
    ॰
    ॰ THE THREE CURSORS SHARE ONE LIFETIME, which is what makes reading them here
    ॰ sound rather than convenient: `आज्ञासूचकाङ्क` (`vakyavibhaga.t1:452`),
    ॰ `दत्तसूचकाङ्क` (`:454`) and `वैश्विकसंख्यानम्` (`:471`) are all cleared in the
    ॰ same reset routine. They cannot drift out of step with each other.
    ॰ The alternative — moving this guard below `कार्यक्रमरचना` to read the
    ॰ record's counts — would run the builder on input this guard currently
    ॰ rejects, and nothing establishes that is harmless.
    यदि वाक्यविभागॱवाक्यविभागआज्ञासूचकाङ्क समम् ० आदि
        यदि वाक्यविभागॱदत्तसूचकाङ्क समम् ० आदि
            यदि वाक्यविभागॱवैश्विकसंख्यानम् समम् ० आदि
                वस्तुरचनाविरामभेद भवति वस्तुरचनारिक्तभेद ।
                प्रत्यागमनम् शून्यम् ।
            इति
        इति
    इति

    चरः कार्यक्रमः ॱॱ वाक्यविभागॱकार्यक्रम भवति वाक्यविभागॱकार्यक्रमरचना ।
    चरः स्थानानि ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ३२ भवति सङ्केतनॱस्थानविन्यासः कार्यक्रमः सङ्केतनॱअसङ्कुचितम् ।
    चरः अष्टकाः ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति सङ्केतनॱवस्तुसङ्केतनम् कार्यक्रमः ।
    ॰ THE REASON IS ALREADY RECORDED ONE LAYER DOWN AND THIS STOPS DISCARDING IT.
    ॰ `लक्ष्यवस्तुसङ्केतनम्` calls `सङ्केतनदोषरचना ० २२ ० ०` before answering
    ॰ `शून्यम्`, so a code, a site and a reason exist that no exit constant
    ॰ carries. This exit NAMES the layer; `सङ्केतनदोष` still holds the why.
    ॰
    ॰ ══ AND IT ASKED THE PAYLOAD, WHICH IS WHY `१००३` OUTLIVED SEVEN RUNGS ══
    ॰ (2026-09-15.) The test here was `यदि अष्टकाः समम् शून्यम्`. A refusal
    ॰ answers `शून्यम्`; a SUCCESS on a module with no instructions answers an
    ॰ EMPTY run; and natively those are the same word. So every data-only module
    ॰ — rung 73's exemplar among them — was reported as "encoding refused" for a
    ॰ compile that refused nothing. `encode.t1`'s own margin measured it: ० failing
    ॰ instructions of ० total, E22 not fired, the seeded diagnostic untouched.
    ॰ Length cannot separate them either: nil and empty both measure ०, by
    ॰ construction rather than by a guard — `खण्डदैर्घ्यरचना`'s old
    ॰ `+ (दैर्घ्यफलम् == ०)` never applied to an `अ८` run, and since `W-355` it
    ॰ applies to no run at all.
    ॰ `सङ्केतनसिद्धम्` is a verdict the emitter CARRIES instead.
    यदि सङ्केतनॱसङ्केतनसिद्धम् समम् असत्यम् आदि
        वस्तुरचनाविरामभेद भवति वस्तुरचनाष्टकभेद ।
        प्रत्यागमनम् शून्यम् ।
    इति
    वस्तुरचनाविरामभेद भवति वस्तुरचनासिद्धभेद ।
    प्रत्यागमनम् सङ्केतनॱवस्तुरचना आरभ्य कार्यक्रमः ऽ स्थानानि ऽ अष्टकाः समाप्तम् ।
इति

॰ one object to an image — link, then write. `संयोजनम्` takes an ARRAY because
॰ a link is whole-program: it gathers every export across every object before
॰ resolving anything, so a one-object link is the general case with one member
॰ and not a special path.
सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः वस्तुप्रतिबिम्बम् आदाय वस्तु ॱॱ वास्तुॱवस्तु ददाति अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ आदि
    चरः वस्तूनि ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः वास्तुॱवस्तु भवति ० ।
    वस्तूनि अङ्कः ० अन्तः भवति वस्तु ।

    चरः संयोजितम् ॱॱ सम्भाव्य संयोजनॱसंयोजितम् भवति संयोजनॱसंयोजनम् वस्तूनि ।
    यदि संयोजितम् समम् शून्यम् आदि
        प्रत्यागमनम् ० ।
    इति

    प्रत्यागमनम् कोशॱप्रतिबिम्बलेखनम् आरभ्य संयोजितम् ॱ पाठ्यम् ऽ संयोजितम् ॱ दत्तम् ऽ संयोजितम् ॱ बीजम् ऽ कोशॱभारस्थानम् समाप्तम् ।
इति

॰ ॥ वस्तुपाठ्यमुद्रणम् ॥ THE OBJECT'S `.text`, OUT THROUGH THE CHANNEL — Stage
॰ B's consumer, and the first thing in this corpus to call `अष्टकॱमुद्रणम्`.
॰
॰ THE CHANNEL LANDED UNUSED. `ir.t1` lowers the call to a store at the UART and
॰ the interpreter intercepts it, but nothing made the call, so the wire had no
॰ traffic. This makes the traffic, and it makes it for the one payload worth
॰ carrying: the octets a compile produced, so that native and interpreted can
॰ be compared BYTE FOR BYTE instead of through a 16-bit checksum.
॰
॰ THE OBJECT, NOT THE IMAGE, AND THE DIFFERENCE IS NOT COSMETIC.
॰ `मण्डलप्रतिबिम्बम्` below answers a linked ELF, which carries the startup and
॰ a layout — real octets that are not this compiler's output. Comparing images
॰ would score those too and report the total as a statement about the compiler.
॰ `वस्तु ॱ पाठ्यम्` is exactly what the back half emitted and nothing else.
॰
॰ THE LOCAL BINDING IS REQUIRED, NOT STYLE. `पाठवस्तुरचना` answers a
॰ `सम्भाव्य वास्तुॱवस्तु`, and a `सम्भाव्य` will not take `ॱ पाठ्यम्` directly;
॰ `संयोजनॱपाठारम्भः` is the corpus's idiom and binds a `वास्तुॱवस्तु` local from
॰ the arena first. Same shape here.
॰
॰ **THE ANSWER IS ० ONLY ON A COMPLETE WRITE, AND A READER MUST CHECK IT.** The
॰ channel is unframed — one octet per call, no length, no terminator — so a run
॰ that dies part way leaves a PREFIX, and a prefix of an object is byte for byte
॰ a SHORTER OBJECT with a plausible first-differing offset. Nothing in the octet
॰ stream can tell the two apart. The finisher status is the only corroboration
॰ the length has, which is why the refusal path answers `१००० योगः` the builder's
॰ own exit code rather than emitting a short stream and answering ०.
॰
॰ EXPECT `१००३` NATIVELY UNTIL CLAUSE NINE CLOSES. `पाठवस्तुरचना` refuses with
॰ `वस्तुरचनाष्टकभेद` on the compiled side today — rung 73 measured it on a
॰ six-line module holding no instructions. A sweep that comes back all-refused
॰ is therefore the MEASURED STATE and not a broken consumer, and it is written
॰ down here so the first sweep's meaning is not decided after seeing it.
सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः वस्तुपाठ्यमुद्रणम् आदाय पाठ्यम् ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ ददाति न६४ आदि
    ॰ THE RESET IS HERE AND NOT LEFT TO THE CALLER, unlike in `मण्डलप्रतिबिम्बम्`
    ॰ — and the difference is that this takes TEXT, so it cannot know whether a
    ॰ front half ran and left `पदविभाग`'s arenas full. Called cold without it the
    ॰ builder faults with `no record carries a member नाम`, which is a routine
    ॰ called outside its sequence and not a defect in the routine. An instrument
    ॰ that needs its caller to remember a step will eventually be called by
    ॰ someone who does not, and the failure would read as a compiler finding.
    चरः तत्परम् ॱॱ न६४ भवति सङ्कलनारम्भः ।
    चरः वस्तु ॱॱ सम्भाव्य वास्तुॱवस्तु भवति पाठवस्तुरचना पाठ्यम् ।
    यदि वस्तु समम् शून्यम् आदि
        प्रत्यागमनम् १००० योगः वस्तुरचनाविरामभेद ।
    इति

    चरः वस्तूनि ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः वास्तुॱवस्तु भवति ० ।
    वस्तूनि अङ्कः ० अन्तः भवति वस्तु ।
    चरः एकम् ॱॱ वास्तुॱवस्तु भवति वस्तूनि अङ्कः ० अन्तः ।
    चरः अष्टकाः ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति एकम् ॱ पाठ्यम् ।

    चरः क्रमः ॱॱ न६४ भवति ० ।
    यावत् क्रमः न्यूनम् अष्टकाः ॱ दैर्घ्य आदि
        चरः अवगणना ॱॱ न६४ भवति अष्टकॱमुद्रणम् अष्टकाः अङ्कः क्रमः अन्तः ।
        क्रमः भवति क्रमः योगः १ ।
    इति

    प्रत्यागमनम् ० ।
इति

॰ THE WHOLE CHAIN, FROM A `.t1` SOURCE TO AN IMAGE THAT RUNS, DRIVEN FROM
॰ `.t1`. `मण्डलसङ्कलनम्` is the front half and answers Sassembly text; this
॰ carries that text through the back half without Rust between any two stages.
सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः मण्डलप्रतिबिम्बम् आदाय मूल ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ ऽ मण्डलनाम ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ ददाति अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ आदि
    चरः पाठ्यम् ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति मण्डलसङ्कलनम् आरभ्य मूल ऽ मण्डलनाम समाप्तम् ।
    यदि पाठ्यम् ॱ दैर्घ्य समम् ० आदि
        प्रत्यागमनम् आरभ्य उक्तम् इति समाप्तम् ।
    इति

    ॰ THE RESET BELONGS *BETWEEN* THE HALVES AND THE DRIVER OWNS IT.
    ॰ `मण्डलसङ्कलनम्` compiles a T1 source and leaves `पदविभाग`'s arenas full of
    ॰ THAT source's tokens. `वाक्यविभागॱसङ्कलनम्` then lexes the Sassembly text
    ॰ into the SAME arenas — one interpreter image, one lexer, one
    ॰ `चिह्नककोश` — so without a reset the assembler reads the compiler's
    ॰ leavings and faults on a record that is not an `आज्ञा`.
    ॰
    ॰ Calling it before the front half instead does not work and looks like it
    ॰ should: the tables are read, then the compiler overwrites what they share.
    ॰ THE ORDER IS front, reset, back — and it is the driver's to get right
    ॰ because the driver is the only thing that knows both halves ran.
    चरः तत्परम् ॱॱ न६४ भवति सङ्कलनारम्भः ।
    चरः वस्तु ॱॱ सम्भाव्य वास्तुॱवस्तु भवति पाठवस्तुरचना पाठ्यम् ।
    यदि वस्तु समम् शून्यम् आदि
        प्रत्यागमनम् आरभ्य उक्तम् इति समाप्तम् ।
    इति

    प्रत्यागमनम् वस्तुप्रतिबिम्बम् वस्तु ।
इति

॰ ॥ मण्डलानिप्रतिबिम्बम् ॥ THE WHOLE CORPUS TO ONE IMAGE, DRIVEN FROM `.t1` —
॰ `W-279`'s remaining acceptance half: *"nothing yet walks all 19 and feeds
॰ each module's output to the next."*
॰
॰ NEITHER PIECE THIS NEEDED WAS NEW, AND THAT IS THE FINDING. `संयोजनम्` has
॰ taken `वस्तूनि ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः वास्तुॱवस्तु` — an ARRAY — since it landed, and
॰ `वस्तुप्रतिबिम्बम्` above builds a ONE-element arena and passes that. The
॰ linker was N-capable and the driver handed it the degenerate case. Twice in
॰ one evening the blocker here was a capability already paid for and unspent;
॰ the other was `यन्त्रारम्भमण्डलोत्सर्जनम्`, below.
॰
॰ THE STARTUP IS OBJECT ZERO AND THAT IS THE WHOLE REASON THE IMAGE RUNS
॰ RATHER THAN MERELY LOADS. `मण्डलप्रतिबिम्बम्` links the module alone, a
॰ module has no `यन्त्रारम्भ`, so `e_entry` lands in a routine body and the
॰ machine halts `BeyondRam`. That was recorded as "no entry point exists" and
॰ the diagnosis was wrong: `यन्त्रोत्सर्जनॱयन्त्रारम्भमण्डलोत्सर्जनम्` emits the
॰ stub and its margin says *"Linked FIRST, so `e_entry` — the image's first
॰ instruction — is `यन्त्रारम्भ`"*. The defect was never a missing entry, it
॰ was a missing OBJECT. A symptom compatible with two causes is not a
॰ diagnosis.
॰
॰ NO ENTRY IS NAMED, DELIBERATELY. `यन्त्रप्रवेशन्यासः` is public and would let
॰ this call a routine, and the stub's own margin says `०` gives an image
॰ "whose stub halts success" — which satisfies RUN. Naming one would make this
॰ the second thing in the tree ever to reference a startup-DEFINED symbol, and
॰ the pre-link closure in `paradigm_encode.rs` is blind to the startup object
॰ (it refuses at `:1246` and pushes the startup at `:1263`). That blindness is
॰ dormant on main only because nothing references such a symbol. ONE NEW
॰ CAPABILITY PER UNIT.
॰
॰ THE CALLER SUPPLIES THE SET AND THAT IS THE CORRECT SIGNATURE, NOT A
॰ SHORTFALL. `cc *.c` is the SHELL globbing and handing over a list; a compiler
॰ does not read directories. Enumeration belongs in the harness, where it can
॰ be counted; compilation belongs here.
॰
॰ THE RESET IS PER SOURCE, for the reason `मण्डलप्रतिबिम्बम्` states: the front
॰ half leaves `पदविभाग`'s arenas full of that source's tokens and the back half
॰ lexes Sassembly into the SAME arenas. `पदविभाग` resets `चिह्नकसूचकाङ्क` on
॰ entry, `अर्थ` and `मध्यरूप` take their own `आरम्भः`, so the front half is
॰ safe to re-enter; it is the ASSEMBLER that needs `सङ्कलनारम्भः` between the
॰ halves, every time round.
॰
॰ A SOURCE THAT DOES NOT COMPILE IS SKIPPED, NOT FATAL. Three of the corpus
॰ declare no routines and emit no object at all — an image of the whole corpus
॰ is the objects the corpus PRODUCES, and refusing everything because
॰ `ast.t1` has no routines would answer nothing about the other seventeen.
सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः प्रवेशन्यासः आदाय मण्डल ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ ऽ वृत्तिनाम ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ ददाति न६४ आदि
    प्रवेशमण्डलम् भवति मण्डल ।
    प्रवेशवृत्तिः भवति वृत्तिनाम ।
    प्रवेशमस्ति भवति सत्यम् ।
    प्रत्यागमनम् वृत्तिनाम ॱ दैर्घ्य ।
इति

॰ THE SELF-HOSTING RUNG WITH NO HARNESS: compile a program held as a literal —
॰ a data-only module, because a literal ends at the first `इति` — and answer
॰ the emitted text's length. Run by the interpreter it predicts the number;
॰ run as the compiled compiler's entry, the image's exit status must equal it.
॰ THE RUNGS BELOW स्वपरीक्षा, for bisecting a native answer that is not the
॰ interpreted one (2026-09-13: the compiled compiler answered 0 where the
॰ interpreter answers 234). Each is an entry; its result is the exit status.
सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः स्वपरीक्षाशून्या ददाति न६४ आदि
    प्रत्यागमनम् ७ ।
