॰ ॥ RUNG 80 — THE COMPILED COMPILER'S OUTPUT, OUT THROUGH THE CHANNEL ॥ (2026-09-18)
॰ The first caller `वस्तुपाठ्यमुद्रणम्` has ever had. That routine was written to
॰ be "Stage B's consumer, and the first thing in this corpus to call
॰ `अष्टकॱमुद्रणम्`" — and then nothing called IT, so the channel landed unused a
॰ second time, one level up.
॰
॰ WHY IT MATTERS MORE THAN ANOTHER RUNG. Every rung below answers a NUMBER, so
॰ native and interpreted are compared through a scalar: equal numbers, unknown
॰ octets. This carries the object's `.text` itself, so the two sides can be
॰ compared BYTE FOR BYTE — what the channel's own margin says it exists for. It
॰ is also the primitive a bootstrap fixpoint's Stage 2 needs: a natively-running
॰ image that compiles a source and emits the result, no Rust between any two
॰ stages.
॰
॰ THE INPUT CARRIES A ROUTINE, AND THE FIRST VERSION DID NOT. It used rung 73's
॰ module — one global, NO ROUTINES — whose `.text` is legitimately EMPTY.
॰ MEASURED 2026-09-18: the image halted `Finisher { status: Some(0) }` having
॰ written ZERO OCTETS, and ० is exactly what a COMPLETE write answers. The status
॰ could not tell "wrote the whole object" from "wrote nothing" — the degenerate
॰ prefix this routine's own margin warns of, and the exit-zero-over-nothing shape
॰ four tools in this project already carry. A payload test whose input has no
॰ payload measures the harness.
॰
॰ SPLIT AROUND `इति`, the idiom rungs 46–47 use: a `उक्तम् … इति` literal ends at
॰ the FIRST `इति`, so an embedded routine's terminator closes the literal early.
॰ Writing it whole took shrinkhala from 101 routines to ० and the census caught
॰ it. Piece one ends `इ`, piece two opens `ति`, `पाठसंयोगः` joins them.
॰
॰ THE PREDICTION THIS REPLACES WAS PRE-REGISTERED AND IS STALE.
॰ `वस्तुपाठ्यमुद्रणम्`'s margin says "EXPECT १००३ NATIVELY UNTIL CLAUSE NINE
॰ CLOSES". Rung 73's margin now records २००० natively as of 2026-09-18: the
॰ refusal is gone, so ० — a complete write — is the registered expectation, and a
॰ १००३ here would mean the refusal came back rather than never having left.
सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः स्वपरीक्षाशीतिः ददाति न६४ आदि
    चरः आरम्भः ॱॱ न६४ भवति सङ्कलनारम्भः ।
    चरः प१ ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति उक्तम् मण्डलम् क ॥ सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः घ ददाति न६४ आदि प्रत्यागमनम् ६ । इ इति ।
    चरः प२ ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति उक्तम् ति इति ।
    चरः मूल ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति पाठसंयोगः आरभ्य प१ ऽ प२ समाप्तम् ।
    चरः पाठ्यम् ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति मण्डलसङ्कलनम् आरभ्य मूल ऽ उक्तम् क इति समाप्तम् ।
    प्रत्यागमनम् वस्तुपाठ्यमुद्रणम् पाठ्यम् ।
इति

॰ ॥ RUNG 81 — THE BACK HALF ON A ROUTINE, WITHOUT THE CHANNEL ॥ (2026-09-18)
॰ Rung 80's fault is now bounded on both sides and this closes the gap.
॰
॰   rung 47  front half, routine-carrying input   NATIVE = INTERPRETED = 1694
॰   rung 73  front+back, NO routine               NATIVE २०००, clean
॰   rung 80  front+back+channel, one routine      NATIVE BadAccess addr ०
॰
॰ So the front half compiles a routine natively and correctly, and the back half
॰ is clean on an input with no instructions. What is untested is the back half ON
॰ instructions — and rung 80 cannot separate that from the channel write, because
॰ it does both.
॰
॰ THIS IS RUNG 79's SHAPE WITH RUNG 47's INPUT: `पाठवस्तुरचना` and then the
॰ object's own `पाठ्यम् ॱ दैर्घ्य`, offset by २००० exactly as 73 and 79 are, and
॰ NO call to `अष्टकॱमुद्रणम्`. A native २०४० says the assembler encoded the
॰ routine and the fault is in the channel; a native fault says the assembler.
॰ १००x says it declined, which is a third answer and not the same as either.
सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः स्वपरीक्षैकाशीतिः ददाति न६४ आदि
    चरः आरम्भः ॱॱ न६४ भवति सङ्कलनारम्भः ।
    चरः प१ ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति उक्तम् मण्डलम् क ॥ सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः घ ददाति न६४ आदि प्रत्यागमनम् ६ । इ इति ।
    चरः प२ ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति उक्तम् ति इति ।
    चरः मूल ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति पाठसंयोगः आरभ्य प१ ऽ प२ समाप्तम् ।
    चरः पाठ्यम् ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति मण्डलसङ्कलनम् आरभ्य मूल ऽ उक्तम् क इति समाप्तम् ।
    चरः फलम् ॱॱ सम्भाव्य वास्तुॱवस्तु भवति पाठवस्तुरचना पाठ्यम् ।
    यदि फलम् समम् शून्यम् आदि
        प्रत्यागमनम् १००० योगः वस्तुरचनाविरामभेद ।
    इति
    चरः वस्तूनि ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः वास्तुॱवस्तु भवति ० ।
    वस्तूनि अङ्कः ० अन्तः भवति फलम् ।
    चरः वस्तु ॱॱ वास्तुॱवस्तु भवति वस्तूनि अङ्कः ० अन्तः ।
    प्रत्यागमनम् २००० योगः वस्तु ॱ पाठ्यम् ॱ दैर्घ्य ।
इति

॰ ॥ RUNG 82 — A PROGRESS MARKER THROUGH THE CHANNEL ॥ (2026-09-18)
॰ Rungs 80 and 81 both fault at `BadAccess addr ०` inside the assembler, and a
॰ fault CANNOT REPORT: the routine never returns, so every code the exit status
॰ could have carried is unreachable. The channel is the only thing that escapes a
॰ run that dies, because each octet leaves the machine as it is written.
॰
॰ THE CHANNEL HAS NEVER BEEN SHOWN TO WORK NATIVELY, and that has to come first
॰ or a silent marker is unreadable. Rung 80's routineless version halted cleanly
॰ having written ZERO octets — it never called the channel at all — and its
॰ routine-carrying version faulted before reaching the write. So `अ` here is a
॰ CONTROL, not a marker: if it does not appear, the instrument is the story and
॰ nothing below it means anything.
॰
॰ THEN ONE OCTET PER STAGE:
॰   अ (65)  the channel works and the rung started
॰   ब (66)  the FRONT half returned — `मण्डलसङ्कलनम्` produced Sassembly text
॰   स (67)  `पाठवस्तुरचना` returned — the assembler survived
॰ Native stdout is then a prefix that names the last stage reached. `अब` and a
॰ fault says the assembler; `अ` alone says the front half, which rung 47 has
॰ already refuted natively, so that outcome would indict this rung instead.
॰
॰ IT ANSWERS २००० + the object's length exactly as rungs 73, 79 and 81 do, so a
॰ COMPLETE run is comparable with them and not a new scale.
सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः स्वपरीक्षाद्व्यशीतिः ददाति न६४ आदि
    चरः आरम्भः ॱॱ न६४ भवति सङ्कलनारम्भः ।
    चरः चिह्नैक ॱॱ न६४ भवति अष्टकॱमुद्रणम् ६५ ।
