॰ ॥ RUNG 86 — DID THE SEED TAKE? ॥ (2026-09-18)
॰ Rung 85 seeded `अन्तिमसङ्केतनदोषः` with `सङ्केतनदोषरचना ० ० ० ०` and faulted at
॰ the SAME 933 octets as rung 84. I read that as refuting the hypothesis. It does
॰ not, and the reason is the oldest one on the list: A FALSIFIER THAT NEVER
॰ CHANGED ITS SUBJECT FALSIFIES NOTHING.
॰
॰ The hypothesis is that a record constructed into a global declared
॰ `सङ्केतनदोष भवति ०` does not stick natively — so `सङ्केतनदोषरचना` is exactly
॰ the operation under suspicion, and rung 85 used it as though it were reliable.
॰ If the construction is the broken thing, the seed was a no-op and rung 85
॰ measured the unseeded case twice.
॰
॰ THIS READS THE FIELD BACK IMMEDIATELY AFTER SEEDING IT, before any compiling
॰ happens, and puts the answer on the channel:
॰
॰   अ ... then (१, पङ्क्ति)   the seed took, and ७७७७ is not where it dies
॰   अ then a FAULT            a field read on a freshly constructed global faults
॰                              natively — which is the defect, reached in four
॰                              statements instead of through a whole compile
॰
॰ EITHER ANSWER IS WORTH THE BUILD, and the second would mean every rung above
॰ has been walking a long way to reach a fault that reproduces immediately.
सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः स्वपरीक्षाषडशीतिः ददाति न६४ आदि
    चरः आरम्भः ॱॱ न६४ भवति सङ्कलनारम्भः ।
    चरः चिह्नैक ॱॱ न६४ भवति अष्टकॱमुद्रणम् ६५ ।
    चरः बीजम् ॱॱ अ६४ भवति सङ्केतनॱसङ्केतनदोषरचना ४२४२ ० ० ० ।
    चरः चिह्नद्वि ॱॱ न६४ भवति अष्टकॱमुद्रणम् ६६ ।
    चरः पठितम् ॱॱ अ६४ भवति सङ्केतनॱअन्तिमसङ्केतनदोषः ॱ पङ्क्ति ।
    चरः चिह्नत्रि ॱॱ न६४ भवति अष्टकॱमुद्रणम् ६७ ।
    प्रत्यागमनम् ३००० योगः पठितम् ।
इति

॰ ॥ RUNG 96 — IS IT THE RECORD, OR IS IT THE CONTEXT? ॥ (2026-09-18)
॰ Rung 95 measured: the SLICE returns and the FIELD WRITE faults —
॰ `नव ॱ आज्ञा भवति आज्ञापाठः` at vishlesana.t1, `नव` being `सङ्केत भवति ०`.
॰
॰ THREE EXPLANATIONS ARE NOW DEAD, ALL KILLED BY RUNG 86 RATHER THAN BY NEW RUNS:
॰   ॱ `कोष्ठाङ्कः` Some(०) — refuted on the code, `… योगः १` keeps ० out of the hole
॰   ॱ a ०-declared record local cannot be written — `सङ्केतनदोषरचना` does it and
॰     answers ७२४२ natively
॰   ॱ a RUN-typed field cannot be written into one — that same routine writes
॰     `नव ॱ सङ्केताङ्क भवति सङ्केतनकूटः सङ्ख्या`, and `सङ्केतनकूटः` answers OCTETS
॰     ("E00"), not a number
॰
॰ So the rule applies and this is a MARKER, not a fourth guess. It splits the two
॰ things that still differ between the routine that works and the one that does
॰ not: the record TYPE, and the CONTEXT it runs in.
॰
॰   faults here  → a `सङ्केत` field write faults on its own, two statements in,
॰                  with nothing else having run. The record type is the subject.
॰   works here   → the operation is fine in isolation and something the COMPILE
॰                  leaves behind breaks it — allocator state after ~232 records
॰                  of encoding, which is a different investigation entirely.
॰
॰ IT WRITES THE SAME FIELD THE FAULTING SITE WRITES, `आज्ञा`, with an octet run,
॰ so the only difference from vishlesana.t1:885 is everything that did NOT happen
॰ before it.
सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः स्वपरीक्षाषण्णवतिः ददाति न६४ आदि
    चरः आरम्भः ॱॱ न६४ भवति सङ्कलनारम्भः ।
    चरः चिह्नैक ॱॱ न६४ भवति अष्टकॱमुद्रणम् ६५ ।
    चरः नव ॱॱ सङ्केतनॱसङ्केत भवति ० ।
    चरः चिह्नद्वि ॱॱ न६४ भवति अष्टकॱमुद्रणम् ६६ ।
    नव ॱ आज्ञा भवति उक्तम् योगः इति ।
    चरः चिह्नत्रि ॱॱ न६४ भवति अष्टकॱमुद्रणम् ६७ ।
    प्रत्यागमनम् ५००० योगः नव ॱ आज्ञा ॱ दैर्घ्य ।
इति

॰ ══ RUNG 103: A MODULE-LEVEL GLOBAL READ, LOWERED NATIVELY ═════════
॰
॰ THE SEVENTH CONSTRUCT, AND THE SECOND THAT IS NOT ON `7319bd11`'s TABLE AT
॰ ALL. Rungs 97 to 101 took the five shapes `spec/demo/` holds and rung 102 took
॰ the cross-module CALL. Every one of those seven sources computes out of
॰ REGISTERS and LITERALS: not one of them touches STORAGE. This is the first rung
॰ whose object has a `.data` section at all, and the first whose answer depends on
॰ the emitter placing a global's octets somewhere and then addressing them.
॰
॰ WHY THIS SHAPE IS AVAILABLE ONLY NOW, STATED AS THE RECORD RATHER THAN AS
॰ CONVENIENCE. Until 2026-09-21 `tools/demo.sh` could not report this source's
॰ counts at all: `crates/frontend/src/pathana.rs` passed `globals: Vec::new()`
॰ and entered no global's SYMBOL into `Names`, so the demo's stage 6 REFUSED
॰ ``symbol SymbolId(2) has no name`` and threw stages 7 and 8 away — *every*
॰ source in the language that reads one of its own module's globals stopped at
॰ stage six. `W-278`'s port opened it and
॰ `crates/frontend/tests/module_globals.rs` is its witness. A rung cannot be
॰ PREDICTED from a stage that does not run, which is why this row is written now
॰ and not beside rung 102.
॰
॰ MEASURED THIS CYCLE ON THE SHORTENED SOURCE, NOT QUOTED. `tools/demo.sh` over
॰ the literal below — and over the same text whitespace-normalised to ONE line,
॰ which is what this routine actually compiles — reports IDENTICALLY: **1
॰ routine, 2 blocks, 3 IR instructions, 0 calls (0 cross-module)**, 0 constants,
॰ 1 arithmetic, 31 lines of T0, twins AGREE on 2158 octets, **1040 octets of
॰ object and 18 machine instructions in `.text`**, and the machine halts with
॰ status १२.
॰
॰ TWO GLOBALS AND NOT ONE, AND THE SECOND IS THE ROW'S OWN CONTROL. The
॰ single-global source `मण्डलम् क ॥ सार्वजनिक चरः ग ॱॱ न६४ भवति ७ । …` measures
॰ 1 IR instruction and **12** machine instructions; this one measures 3 and 18.
॰ The difference is SIX, which is 3 per global read (`स्थानसापेक्षयोगः`, `योगः`
॰ against the low half, `आहारः`) plus one `निधानम्` spill and one `आहारः` reload
॰ for the extra live value and one `योगः` for the add. A rung on the one-global
॰ source could not tell a table with ONE reachable entry from a table, which is
॰ the defect `module_globals.rs`'s third property exists to refuse; two globals
॰ with DIFFERENT initialisers make the count and the answer both move.
॰
॰ TWO PIECES AND ONE JOIN — the fewest on the ladder, tied with rung 102. The
॰ literal `उक्तम् … इति` ends at the WORD `इति` and this module has exactly ONE
॰ standalone `इति`, the one closing `घ` — the two `चरः` declarations end in `।`.
॰ The split was checked by reassembly BEFORE this routine was written: the two
॰ piece strings concatenate character for character to the whitespace-normalised
॰ source (`MATCH: True`), and neither piece contains `इति` as a word. `ॱ` survives
॰ inside a literal — rung 101's piece 2 carries `ॱॱ` — so the `ॱॱ` in
॰ `चरः ग ॱॱ न६४` needs no splitting.
॰
॰ IT ANSWERS ११००० PLUS THE OBJECT'S TEXT LENGTH, AND ११००० WAS CHOSEN BY
॰ GREPPING THIS FILE: `प्रत्यागमनम् <four or more digits> योगः` returns १०००,
॰ २०००, ३०००, ४०००, ५०००, ६०००, ७०००, ८०००, ९००० and १०००० AND NOTHING ELSE, so
॰ an empty object answers exactly ११००० and cannot be read as rung 97's ३११६,
॰ rung 98's ४१६४, rung 99's ६११६, rung 100's ८१७६, rung 101's ९१५६ or rung 102's
॰ १००५२.
॰
॰ PREDICTED BEFORE THE IMAGE EXISTS: **११०७२**. 18 instructions are 72 octets,
॰ and four-octets-per-instruction is not an assumption — it is what the six
॰ ANSWERED rungs measured (29→११६ twice, 41→१६४, 44→८१७६, 39→९१५६, 13→१००५२) and
॰ the layout is `सङ्केतनॱअसङ्कुचितम्`, so no instruction has a two-octet form.
॰
॰ THE FALSIFIERS, REGISTERED HERE AND NOT ONLY IN THE LEDGER:
॰   ११००० alone — the object came back EMPTY; that is the E02 shape.
॰   strictly between ११००० and ११०७२ — should be IMPOSSIBLE, because the encoder
॰     returns `शून्यम्` on refusal and the object is all or nothing. Such a status
॰     overturns THAT reading of `उत्सर्जनक्रमः`, not this rung.
॰   BELOW ११०७२ AND ABOVE ११००० IS THE ONE THIS ROW ADDS, AND IT IS THE
॰     INTERESTING DIRECTION — every rung before this one could only be surprised
॰     UPWARD. ११०४८ is 12 instructions, which is the ONE-GLOBAL count, and
॰     ११०२४ or thereabouts is what a CONSTANT FOLD looks like: a compiled emitter
॰     that answered the declaration's initialiser instead of loading the storage
॰     drops the three-instruction address-and-load sequence per global and the
॰     count falls. That is precisely the defect
॰     `the_status_moves_with_the_globals_initialiser` guards on the Rust side and
॰     no rung has ever been able to see it, because no rung before this one read
॰     anything out of memory.
॰   above ११०७२ — the compiled emitter placed MORE than the Rust chain did. For a
॰     global read that means the `स्थानसापेक्षयोगः`/`योगः` pair against the
॰     symbol's upper and lower halves was relaxed to a wider form, or the `.data`
॰     octets were counted into the text.
॰   ११०७२ WITH A DIVERGING TRACE IS NOT A PASS. The status is a LENGTH and a
॰     right length by coincidence has already happened once on this ladder —
॰     rung 99's ११६ was also rung 97's. The record-by-record diff against the
॰     interpreted sink is the result; the scalar is not.
॰   and a StepLimit in the runner's `.err` is not an answer at all — the ceiling
॰     is the runner's, not the machine's.
॰
॰ AND THE LIMIT IS NAMED RATHER THAN COVERED BY THE RESULT, THE SAME WAY RUNG
॰ 102's LINK LABEL WAS. What this rung CANNOT see is WHICH STORAGE EACH LOAD
॰ ADDRESSES. `कग` and `कच` are both eight octets, so an emitter that addressed
॰ `कग` twice would place the same 18 instructions and answer ११०७२ — and would
॰ compute १४, not १२. The status here is a LENGTH, not the program's answer, so
॰ the ADDRESSES rest where `module_globals.rs` left them: on `tools/demo.sh`,
॰ which is the RUST chain. Engine agreement is what this row proves; the two
॰ labels `कग` and `कच` are proved elsewhere.
सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः स्वपरीक्षात्रिशततमी ददाति न६४ आदि
    चरः आरम्भः ॱॱ न६४ भवति सङ्कलनारम्भः ।
    चरः चिह्नैक ॱॱ न६४ भवति अष्टकॱमुद्रणम् ६५ ।
    चरः प१ ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति उक्तम् मण्डलम् क ॥ सार्वजनिक चरः ग ॱॱ न६४ भवति ७ । सार्वजनिक चरः च ॱॱ न६४ भवति ५ । सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः घ ददाति न६४ आदि प्रत्यागमनम् ग योगः च । इ इति ।
    चरः प२ ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति उक्तम् ति इति ।
    चरः मूल ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति पाठसंयोगः आरभ्य प१ ऽ प२ समाप्तम् ।
    चरः पाठ्यम् ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति मण्डलसङ्कलनम् आरभ्य मूल ऽ उक्तम् क इति समाप्तम् ।
    चरः चिह्नद्वि ॱॱ न६४ भवति अष्टकॱमुद्रणम् ६६ ।
    चरः वाक्यानि ॱॱ न६४ भवति वाक्यविभागॱसङ्कलनम् पाठ्यम् ।
    चरः चिह्नत्रि ॱॱ न६४ भवति अष्टकॱमुद्रणम् ६७ ।
    चरः कार्यक्रमः ॱॱ वाक्यविभागॱकार्यक्रम भवति वाक्यविभागॱकार्यक्रमरचना ।
    चरः चिह्नचतुर् ॱॱ न६४ भवति अष्टकॱमुद्रणम् ६८ ।
    चरः स्थानानि ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ३२ भवति सङ्केतनॱस्थानविन्यासः कार्यक्रमः सङ्केतनॱअसङ्कुचितम् ।
    चरः चिह्नपञ्च ॱॱ न६४ भवति अष्टकॱमुद्रणम् ६९ ।
    चरः स्विचः ॱॱ न६४ भवति सङ्केतनॱविन्यासमुद्रणारम्भः सत्यम् ।
    चरः अष्टकाः ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति सङ्केतनॱवस्तुसङ्केतनम् कार्यक्रमः ।
    चरः चिह्नषट् ॱॱ न६४ भवति अष्टकॱमुद्रणम् ७० ।
    प्रत्यागमनम् ११००० योगः अष्टकाः ॱ दैर्घ्य ।
इति

॰ ══ RUNG 102: A CALL INTO ANOTHER MODULE, LOWERED NATIVELY ════════
॰
॰ THE SIXTH CONSTRUCT, AND THE FIRST ONE THAT IS NOT ON `7319bd11`'s TABLE AT
॰ ALL. Rungs 97 to 101 took the five shapes `spec/demo/` holds — a call, a
॰ branch, a loop, recursion, a two-armed branch over arithmetic. Every one of
॰ those calls, branches and loops stays INSIDE one module, and every one of the
॰ five rows carries `0 cross-module` in its margin. This is the shape those six
॰ margins are the absence of: `आयातः <module> ।` and a callee named
॰ `<module>ॱ<member>`, which the corpus makes 1,105 of and which no rung has
॰ asked the compiled emitter to place.
॰
॰ ONE FILE IS ONE MODULE, so the callee is NOT in the literal. Measured
॰ 2026-09-20: all 21 corpus sources and all six of `spec/demo/` declare exactly
॰ one `मण्डलम्`, and a second declaration is not a shape the parser has. So the
॰ literal IMPORTS `अष्टक` and calls `अष्टकॱशून्याष्टकयोजनम्`, which `ashtaka.t1`
॰ really does export and whose signature really is `न६४ → न६४`.
॰
॰ MEASURED THIS CYCLE ON THE SHORTENED SOURCE, NOT QUOTED: `tools/demo.sh` over
॰ it reports **1 routine, 2 blocks, 2 IR instructions, 1 call — AND THE CALL IS
॰ `1 cross-module`** — 1 constant (1 non-zero), 0 arithmetic, 20 lines of T0,
॰ twins AGREE on 1438 octets, **960 octets of object and 13 machine instructions
॰ in `.text`**. It is the SHORTEST source on the ladder by every count.
॰
॰ THE `1` IS A MEASUREMENT AND NOT A READING, AND THAT IS NEW THIS CYCLE. Until
॰ `W-279`'s previous cycle that counter read `0` for every input in the tree —
॰ `kosha.t1`'s forty cross-module calls included — so the five rows above were
॰ each written from an instrument with ONE reachable state.
॰ `crates/frontend/tests/cross_module_calls.rs` holds the four properties
॰ that made it two, and this literal is the shape its first property asserts.
॰
॰ AND THE ASSEMBLE COUNTS WERE UNOBTAINABLE UNTIL THIS CYCLE, WHICH IS WHY THIS
॰ RUNG COULD NOT BE PREDICTED BEFORE. `tools/demo.sh` printed
॰ `7-8 REFUSED — at LINK: …` for exactly this source and threw stage 7's two
॰ numbers away, HAVING COMPUTED THEM. A four-stage back half reported two
॰ outcomes where the truth has three, and the third is the one every
॰ cross-module source takes. It prints `7 ASSEMBLE ok` and then `8 REFUSED` now.
॰
॰ TWO PIECES AND ONE JOIN — THE FEWEST ON THE LADDER, AND THE COUNT WAS TAKEN
॰ FROM THIS SOURCE RATHER THAN FROM THE ROW ABOVE. The literal `उक्तम् … इति`
॰ ends at the WORD `इति` and this module has exactly ONE standalone `इति`, the
॰ one closing `घ` — rung 100 has three and rung 101 has four. Copying either
॰ split here would bind names to pieces that do not exist. The split was checked
॰ by reassembly BEFORE this routine was written: the two piece strings
॰ concatenate character for character to the whitespace-normalised source
॰ (`MATCH: True`), and neither piece contains `इति` as a word. `ॱ` survives
॰ inside a literal — rung 101's own piece 2 carries `ॱॱ` — so
॰ `अष्टकॱशून्याष्टकयोजनम्` needs no splitting.
॰
॰ IT ANSWERS १०००० PLUS THE OBJECT'S LENGTH, AND १०००० WAS CHOSEN BY GREPPING
॰ THIS FILE: `प्रत्यागमनम् <four or more digits> योगः` returns १०००, २०००,
॰ ३०००, ४०००, ५०००, ६०००, ७०००, ८००० and ९००० and NOTHING WITH FIVE DIGITS, so
॰ an empty object answers exactly १०००० and cannot be read as rung 97's ३११६,
॰ rung 98's ४१६४, rung 99's ६११६, rung 100's ८१७६ or rung 101's ९१५६.
॰
॰ PREDICTED BEFORE THE IMAGE EXISTS: **१००५२**. 13 instructions are 52 octets,
॰ and four-octets-per-instruction is not an assumption — it is what the five
॰ ANSWERED rungs measured (29→११६ twice, 41→१६४, 44→८१७६, 39→९१५६) and the
॰ layout is `सङ्केतनॱअसङ्कुचितम्`, so no instruction has a two-octet form.
॰
॰ THE FALSIFIERS, REGISTERED HERE AND NOT ONLY IN THE LEDGER:
॰   १०००० alone — the object came back EMPTY; that is the E02 shape.
॰   strictly between १०००० and १००५२ — should be IMPOSSIBLE, because the
॰     encoder returns `शून्यम्` on refusal and the object is all or nothing.
॰     Such a status overturns THAT reading of `उत्सर्जनक्रमः`, not this rung.
॰   above १००५२ — the compiled emitter placed MORE than the Rust chain did.
॰     For a cross-module call that means the edge to a label NO object in this
॰     unit defines was relaxed to a wider form. It is the one edge on this
॰     ladder whose displacement is UNKNOWN at layout time, which is precisely
॰     the property the rung is here to test: an intra-module call's target is in
॰     the same `.text` and its displacement is computable, a cross-module call's
॰     is a relocation the linker resolves later.
॰   AND THE ONE THIS ROW ADDS TO THE LADDER, WHICH THE SCALAR CANNOT SEE: A
॰     CROSS-MODULE CALL LOWERED AS AN INTRA-MODULE ONE WOULD STILL ANSWER
॰     १००५२. Two things say this source tests what it claims and BOTH are in
॰     the margin above: `1 cross-module` from `tools/demo.sh`, and THE LINK
॰     LABEL — a correct lowering names `अष्टकशून्याष्टकयोजनम्`, the DEFINING
॰     module's export, and the pre-`W-253` wrong one names `कसंज्ञा<id>`, a name
॰     minted inside the resolving program that nothing can export. The label is
॰     the stronger of the two because it is a NAME and not a count.
॰   १००५२ WITH A DIVERGING TRACE IS NOT A PASS. The status is a LENGTH and a
॰     right length by coincidence has already happened once on this ladder —
॰     rung 99's ११६ was also rung 97's. The record-by-record diff against the
॰     interpreted sink is the result; the scalar is not.
॰   and a StepLimit in the runner's `.err` is not an answer at all — the
॰     ceiling is the runner's, not the machine's.
॰
॰ ONE THING TO EXPECT THAT NO RUNG BEFORE IT HAD: THE LITERAL WILL NOT LINK,
॰ AND THAT IS CORRECT. The rung stops at `सङ्केतनॱवस्तुसङ्केतनम्` and returns
॰ the OBJECT's length; it never links. Anyone checking the source with
॰ `tools/demo.sh` first sees `8 REFUSED — at LINK: अष्टकशून्याष्टकयोजनम् is
॰ not defined by any object`, because the demo compiles ONE file. Read the
॰ LABEL, not the refusal.
॰
॰ AND `आयातः` IS LOAD-BEARING, MEASURED RATHER THAN ASSUMED. With that one line
॰ deleted and nothing else changed, the chain REFUSES at RESOLVE —
॰ ``अष्टकॱशून्याष्टकयोजनम्` at line 3 has no declaration`. So the resolver does
॰ consult the import list; what it does NOT check is that the module really
॰ exports the member, which LINK is what catches. That is `W-253`'s design and
॰ it is now a measurement: a literal importing a module that does not exist at
॰ all (`आयातः ख ।`, callee `खॱच`) also reaches ASSEMBLE, with the SAME 13
॰ instructions and the label `खच`. Two label lengths, one instruction count —
॰ which is the ladder's standing claim that the count is not a function of the
॰ labels, taken here as a control rather than repeated as prose.
सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः स्वपरीक्षाद्विशततमी ददाति न६४ आदि
    चरः आरम्भः ॱॱ न६४ भवति सङ्कलनारम्भः ।
    चरः चिह्नैक ॱॱ न६४ भवति अष्टकॱमुद्रणम् ६५ ।
    चरः प१ ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति उक्तम् मण्डलम् क ॥ आयातः अष्टक । सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः घ ददाति न६४ आदि प्रत्यागमनम् अष्टकॱशून्याष्टकयोजनम् ७ । इ इति ।
    चरः प२ ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति उक्तम् ति इति ।
    चरः मूल ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति पाठसंयोगः आरभ्य प१ ऽ प२ समाप्तम् ।
    चरः पाठ्यम् ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति मण्डलसङ्कलनम् आरभ्य मूल ऽ उक्तम् क इति समाप्तम् ।
    चरः चिह्नद्वि ॱॱ न६४ भवति अष्टकॱमुद्रणम् ६६ ।
    चरः वाक्यानि ॱॱ न६४ भवति वाक्यविभागॱसङ्कलनम् पाठ्यम् ।
    चरः चिह्नत्रि ॱॱ न६४ भवति अष्टकॱमुद्रणम् ६७ ।
    चरः कार्यक्रमः ॱॱ वाक्यविभागॱकार्यक्रम भवति वाक्यविभागॱकार्यक्रमरचना ।
    चरः चिह्नचतुर् ॱॱ न६४ भवति अष्टकॱमुद्रणम् ६८ ।
    चरः स्थानानि ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ३२ भवति सङ्केतनॱस्थानविन्यासः कार्यक्रमः सङ्केतनॱअसङ्कुचितम् ।
    चरः चिह्नपञ्च ॱॱ न६४ भवति अष्टकॱमुद्रणम् ६९ ।
    चरः स्विचः ॱॱ न६४ भवति सङ्केतनॱविन्यासमुद्रणारम्भः सत्यम् ।
