॰ ══ RUNG 101: A BRANCH WITH BOTH ARMS OVER AN ARITHMETIC TEST ══════
॰
॰ THE FIFTH CONSTRUCT ON THE LADDER `7319bd11` MEASURED, and the LAST written
॰ row of that table that had never been built. `spec/demo/समविषमम्.t1` is the
॰ BRANCH-DENSE one: **8 blocks on 11 IR instructions** — the MOST blocks and
॰ the FEWEST instructions of any source on the ladder after the fixture. Rung
॰ 98 is also a `यदि`, and this is not rung 98 again for two reasons that are
॰ in the counts rather than in the prose:
॰
॰   ॱ rung 98's `यदि` has NO `अन्यथा`. Its false path falls through to the
॰     statement after the branch. This one has BOTH arms and each arm RETURNS,
॰     so the emitter places two exits and a join that no arm reaches — eight
॰     blocks where rung 98 has seven, on ELEVEN instructions where rung 98 has
॰     twelve. Blocks per instruction is the highest on the ladder.
॰   ॱ this is the FIRST source on the ladder whose CONDITION is an arithmetic
॰     EXPRESSION — `आरभ्य स शेषः २ समाप्तम् समम् ०` — rather than a comparison
॰     of a name against a literal. `शेषः` is the operator this demo's own
॰     margin says it was the first program ever to ask the chain for.
॰
॰ MEASURED THIS CYCLE, NOT QUOTED: `tools/demo.sh` over the shortened source
॰ below reports **2 routines, 8 blocks, 11 IR instructions, 1 call (0
॰ cross-module), 5 constants (3 non-zero), 54 lines of T0, twins AGREE, 1264
॰ octets of object, 39 machine instructions in .text**, and the machine halts
॰ with status १ — seven is odd. `spec/demo/समविषमम्.t1` unshortened reports
॰ every one of those counts identically and an object of 1624 octets; only the
॰ LABEL strings differ, and the instruction count is not a function of them.
॰
॰ FIVE PIECES AND FOUR JOINS — ONE MORE JOIN THAN EVERY RUNG BEFORE IT, AND
॰ THE EXTRA PIECE IS THE EASY ONE TO MISS. The literal `उक्तम् … इति` ends at
॰ the WORD `इति`, so EVERY standalone `इति` must be split `इ` + `ति` — not
॰ only the ones that close a routine. This module has FOUR: one closing `घ`,
॰ one in `इति अन्यथा आदि` closing the TAKEN arm, one closing the `अन्यथा`
॰ arm, and one closing `ङ`. Rung 100's margin says THREE and that is true of
॰ rung 100, whose `यदि` has no `अन्यथा`; COPYING ITS FOUR-PIECE SPLIT HERE
॰ TERMINATES THE LITERAL AT `इति अन्यथा` and drops everything after it.
॰ `पाठसंयोगः` joins two at a time, so four joins and four bound names.
॰
॰ IT ANSWERS ९००० PLUS THE OBJECT'S LENGTH, and ९००० WAS CHOSEN BY GREPPING
॰ THIS FILE rather than by counting upward: `प्रत्यागमनम् <four digits> योगः`
॰ returns १०००, २०००, ३०००, ४०००, ५०००, ६०००, ७००० and ८००० and nothing else,
॰ so an empty object answers exactly ९००० and cannot be read as rung 97's
॰ ३११६, rung 98's ४१६४, rung 99's ६११६ or rung 100's ८१७६.
॰
