॰ ══ RUNG 100: RECURSION — a routine that calls ITSELF, natively ═════
॰
॰ THE FOURTH CONSTRUCT ON THE LADDER `7319bd11` MEASURED, and the first one
॰ whose call graph has a CYCLE. Rung 97 lowered a call (one routine to
॰ another), rung 98 a branch whose arms both return, rung 99 a loop with a
॰ backward edge INSIDE one routine. This is a backward edge THROUGH THE CALL
॰ MECHANISM: `spec/demo/क्रमगुणितम्.t1` is 2 routines, 7 blocks, 14 IR
॰ instructions and **TWO calls — the only source on that table with two** —
॰ and the second of the two is the routine calling itself with a smaller
॰ argument. 44 machine instructions through the Rust chain; the machine halts
॰ with status १२०, which is ५!.
॰
॰ WHY IT IS NOT RUNG 97 AND RUNG 98 ALREADY TAKEN TOGETHER. A recursive call
॰ is the one call shape where the callee's frame is LIVE while the caller's
॰ frame is live, so the saved-register discipline and the return-address slot
॰ have to be right at two depths at once rather than one. The emitted T0 says
॰ it in four lines inside `ङ` alone — `निधानम् स्तूपसूचकःय् ४०न पुनःस्थानम्न`
॰ before the self-call and `आहारः पुनःस्थानम्म् स्तूपसूचकःत् ४०न` after it,
॰ around `लङ्घनम् पुनःस्थानम्म् कङय् ।`, a call to the label the object is
॰ CURRENTLY INSIDE. Rung 97's callee saves nothing across its call because it
॰ makes none. Nothing on this ladder has yet asked the compiled emitter to
॰ spill a live value across a call it places itself.
॰
॰ THE SHORTENED SOURCE MEASURES THE SAME, and that was checked before this
॰ rung was written rather than assumed: the demo over the shortened form
॰ (module `क`, routines `घ`/`ङ`, parameter `स`) reports the same 2 routines,
॰ 7 blocks, 14 instructions, 2 calls and 44 machine instructions, twins
॰ agreeing, and the same status १२०. Renaming moves the LABELS, which are
॰ shorter here, and the object's instruction count is not a function of them.
॰
॰ FOUR PIECES, because this module has THREE bare `इति` — one closing `घ`,
॰ one closing the `यदि`, one closing `ङ` — exactly rung 98's count, and the
॰ literal ends at the first. Each is split `इ` + `ति` so no piece terminates
॰ early, and `पाठसंयोगः` joins two at a time, so three joins. `भवति` and `।`
॰ inside a piece do NOT terminate it: the literal ends at the WORD `इति`.
॰
॰ IT ANSWERS ८००० PLUS THE OBJECT'S LENGTH. २०००, ३०००, ४०००, ५०००, ६०००
॰ and ७००० are all taken by rungs already answered, and १००० is the
॰ `वस्तुरचनाविरामभेद` refusal prefix, so an empty object answers exactly
॰ ८००० and cannot be read as any of them.
॰
॰ `W-279`, 2026-09-22: the `.t1` chain now emits 43 and answers **८१७२** —
॰ see the block at rung 98 for why. The prediction below is the RUST chain's.
॰
॰ PREDICTED BEFORE THE IMAGE EXISTS, AND THE FALSIFIERS WITH IT: **८१७६**.
॰ 44 instructions are 176 octets, and the four-octets-per-instruction reading
॰ is not an assumption here — it is what the three answered rungs of this
॰ ladder measured: rung 97 and rung 99 each assembled 29 instructions and
॰ each answered ११६, and rung 98 assembled 41 and answered १६४.
॰   ८००० alone  — the object came back EMPTY; that is the E02 shape.
॰   strictly between ८००० and ८१७६ — should be IMPOSSIBLE, because the
॰     encoder returns `शून्यम्` on refusal and the object is all or nothing.
॰     Such a status overturns that reading of `उत्सर्जनक्रमः`, not this rung.
॰   above ८१७६ — the compiled emitter placed MORE than the Rust chain did.
॰     For a self-call that means the relaxation did not converge around an
॰     edge whose target is the routine's own entry, which is the one edge on
॰     this ladder whose displacement is known before relaxation starts.
॰   ८१७६ with a trace that DIVERGES — the status is a length and 176 is
॰     reachable by more than one program, so the record-by-record diff is the
॰     result and the scalar is not. Rung 99's record is explicit that 116 was
॰     also rung 97's length and a right length by coincidence is not a pass.
