    चरः चिह्नान्तः ॱॱ न६४ भवति अष्टकॱमुद्रणम् २२३ ।
    यदि अष्टकाः ॱ दैर्घ्य समम् ० आदि
        प्रत्यागमनम् ११०१ ।
    इति
    प्रत्यागमनम् ११०० ।
इति

॰ ══ THE FIXPOINT RUNG: THE COMPILER BUILDS ITS OWN IMAGE (`स्वपरीक्षास्वप्रतिबिम्बम्`) ══
॰
॰ `मण्डलानिप्रतिबिम्बम्` compiles every source and LINKS them into an image; it
॰ is what `t1_image` runs, interpreted, to make Stage 1. This rung runs it on
॰ the SAME sources, fed through the input channel, and prints the image octets
॰ to the sink between markers २३० and २३१. Run natively by Stage 1, what it
॰ prints IS Stage 2 — and if Stage 2 equals Stage 1 octet for octet, then
॰ Stage 3 (Stage 2 on the same input) must equal both, because it is the same
॰ deterministic binary on the same input. That is the fixpoint.
॰
॰ ITS ENTRY IS ITSELF. Stage 1 is built with this rung as its entry, so the
॰ image it builds must name the same entry or Stage 2 could not be Stage 1.
॰ `प्रवेशन्यासः` is called here exactly as `t1_image` calls it before its build.
॰
॰ THE CORPUS ARRIVES AS ONE FILE, `name NUL text NUL` repeated, packed by
॰ `tools/pack-corpus.py` with names derived the way `t1_image` derives them.
॰ NUL never occurs in UTF-8 source, so the split below needs no escaping.
॰
॰ EACH PIECE IS A FRESH DECLARATION, NOT A REASSIGNMENT. `भवति ०` is read
॰ through the declared type only in a DECLARATION; assigned, it is the integer
॰ ०, and the first indexed write into it refuses. So `नाम` and `पाठ` are
॰ declared inside the loop, and each iteration begins with an empty run.
॰
॰ १२०० built · १२०१ built an EMPTY image · १२०२ no input arrived
सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः स्वपरीक्षास्वप्रतिबिम्बम् ददाति न६४ आदि
    यदि निवेशानुरेखणम् समम् १ आदि
        चरः स्विचः ॱॱ न६४ भवति सङ्केतनॱविन्यासमुद्रणारम्भः सत्यम् ।
    इति
    ॰ LEVEL २: each module's generated text instead of the encoder's markers.
    यदि निवेशानुरेखणम् समम् २ आदि
        पाठमुद्रणार्हम् भवति सत्यम् ।
    इति
    चरः दैर्घ्यम् ॱॱ न६४ भवति निवेशपाठः ॱ दैर्घ्य ।
    यदि दैर्घ्यम् समम् ० आदि
        प्रत्यागमनम् १२०२ ।
